\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122427\",\"bodyHead\":\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub> Retain the cached plan when entitlement refresh fails** When an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the pl\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRq\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/components/record/recent.store.ts\",\"line\":128,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891122429,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\",\"bodyHead\":\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub> Map combination recents to the space table** For Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \\\"search\\\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, bu\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRr\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\",\"line\":66,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891122431,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122431\",\"bodyHead\":\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub> Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode** When a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRs\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\",\"line\":28,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891122432,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122432\",\"bodyHead\":\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub> Recompute network state after reconnecting** If Sync Settings is mounted while the browser is offline and then the connection returns, `isNetworkInducedO\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlm3M\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/layout/layers/cache/InMemoryCache.svelte\",\"line\":20,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891138516,\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:25:45Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891138516\",\"bodyHead\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_ <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary> 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -euo pipefail ast-grep outline client/components/collection/CollectionCache.svelt\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlm3Q\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/stores/uiState/uiState.store.ts\",\"line\":182,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891138521,\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:25:45Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891138521\",\"bodyHead\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_ <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary> 🏁 Script executed: ```shell printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable repository guidance ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dloMk\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\",\"line\":1235,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891146946,\"author\":\"pullfrog\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146946\",\"bodyHead\":\"Sessionless `PointLog` rows now receive a `sessionId`, but the import payload never creates the corresponding `session`. The remote schema enforces this required foreign key, and legacy streak rows concretely omit `sessionId`, so their reco\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dloMm\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/stores/datafn.store.ts\",\"line\":871,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891146948,\"author\":\"pullfrog\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146948\",\"bodyHead\":\"If disabled metadata was written, clone-up fails, and this restore write also fails, the live context and local settings have already returned to E2EE while remote authority remains disabled. The next online initialization trusts that remot\"}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dloMq\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/stores/preferences/preferences.store.ts\",\"line\":74,\"latest\":{\"databaseId\":3891146954,\"author\":\"pullfrog\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146954\",\"bodyHead\":\"The value comparison cannot distinguish two in-flight saves of the same key and value. If the first fails after the second is registered, its rollback deletes the newer pending entry and restores stale signal state until that second mutatio\"}}]}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"unresolvedCount\":50,\"outdatedCount\":12,\"newComments\":[{\"threadId\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRp\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\",\"line\":178,\"databaseId\":3891122427,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the cached plan when entitlement refresh fails**\\n\\nWhen an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the plan endpoint is temporarily unavailable, the account update immediately above has already cleared the cached plan and this condition treats the missing response as a failed entitlement. Entitled Nucleum users are consequently redirected to access denied despite the newly persisted `USER_PLAN`; fall back to that validated cached plan on refresh failures while continuing to deny a known non-Nucleum plan.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122427\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\"},{\"threadId\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRq\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/components/record/recent.store.ts\",\"line\":128,\"databaseId\":3891122429,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table**\\n\\nFor Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \\\"search\\\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compatibility mapping already used elsewhere.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\"},{\"threadId\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRr\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\",\"line\":66,\"databaseId\":3891122431,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode**\\n\\nWhen a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude `sync-direct` here or make the flow enable offlinability before setup.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122431\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\"},{\"threadId\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRs\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\",\"line\":28,\"databaseId\":3891122432,\"author\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\"body\":\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Recompute network state after reconnecting**\\n\\nIf Sync Settings is mounted while the browser is offline and then the connection returns, `isNetworkInducedOfflineMode` remains the mount-time value `true`. Although `BaseLayer` updates `$context.isInOfflineMode` to false, this new toggle therefore stays disabled until the settings component is remounted, preventing the user from changing offline availability after reconnecting. Derive this value from reactive connectivity state rather than the fixed `navigator.onLine` snapshot.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122432\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\"commit\":\"0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2\"},{\"threadId\":\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlm3M\",\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"client/layout/layers/cache/InMemoryCache.svelte\",\"line\":20,\"databaseId\":3891138516,\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nast-grep outline client/components/collection/CollectionCache.svelte --items all\\nrg -n -C 6 'collectionStore|linker|refreshCollectionItemCounts|refreshTypedCollections' \\\\\\n  client/components/collection/CollectionCache.svelte\\nrg -n -C 6 'addDatafnRecordToCollection|relateDatafnRecords|collectionStore|linker' \\\\\\n  client/stores/actionMap.ts client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\\n```\\n\\nRepository: 21nCo/nucleum\\n\\nLength of output: 6328\\n\\n---\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- CollectionCache.svelte ---'\\ncat -n client/components/collection/CollectionCache.svelte | sed -n '1,180p'\\n\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- collection store definitions and mutation paths ---'\\nrg -n -C 8 'export (const|let) collectionStore|class .*Collection|collectionStore\\\\s*=|function (insert|update|delete).*collection|collectionStore\\\\.(insert|update|delete|selectMany)' \\\\\\n  client/components/collection client/stores client/products\\n\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- linker definition and mutation paths ---'\\nrg -n -C 8 'export (const|let) linker|class .*Link|linker\\\\s*=|linker\\\\.(insert|update|delete|selectMany)|LinkType\\\\.DIRECT' \\\\\\n  client/products/memotron/linking client/stores\\n\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- active product context and cache mount ---'\\nrg -n -C 5 '\\\\$appStore\\\\.product|Product\\\\.NUCLEUS|Product\\\\.MEMOTRON|resourceCacheComponentKey\\\\(Resource\\\\.collection\\\\)|CollectionCache' \\\\\\n  client/products client/layout client | head -240\\n```\\n\\nRepository: 21nCo/nucleum\\n\\nLength of output: 45574\\n\\n---\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\np