ame\": \"dev\",\n    \"headRefName\": \"codex/tidy-442-04-client-runtime-auth\",\n    \"headRefOid\": \"ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b\",\n    \"mergeStateStatus\": \"UNSTABLE\",\n    \"mergeable\": \"MERGEABLE\",\n    \"number\": 570,\n    \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n    \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:56:05Z\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570\"\n  },\n  \"counts\": {\n    \"reviewThreads\": 126,\n    \"unresolvedThreads\": 53,\n    \"unresolvedCurrentThreads\": 38,\n    \"reviews\": 44,\n    \"issueComments\": 8,\n    \"inlineComments\": 140,\n    \"threadsWithOver100Comments\": 0\n  },\n  \"unresolvedThreads\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY5j3\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 554,\n      \"originalLine\": 430,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201424\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep Flux initialized until all product stores migrate**\\n\\nIn the normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron app flow, this now initializes only DataFn, while numerous unchanged product stores still call the exported legacy `flux` instance—for example, `ResourceStore.create()` invokes `flux.mutation()` and node/history code invokes `flux.selectMany()`. That export remains a null cast until `initFlux()` runs, and repo-wide search shows initialization now occurs only in sheet and extension flows, so ordinary create, edit, and select interactions fail at runtime even though DataFn startup succeeds. Keep the compatibility runtime initialized or migrate every remaining consumer in the same change.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L80-L83](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L80-L83)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY5j4\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/account.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 420,\n      \"originalLine\": 370,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201425\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clear DataFn data before destroying the runtime**\\n\\nWhen AuthFn account deletion succeeds, `signOut()` first calls `destroyNucleumDatafn()`, which clears `runtimeStore`; the following `clearDatafnLocalData()` immediately returns because there is no `runtime?.storage`. Consequently, deleting an account leaves its IndexedDB cache and user data on the device. Clear the active storage before signing out, or retain the storage handle through deletion.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY5j5\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/account/auth.ts\",\n      \"line\": 238,\n      \"originalLine\": 275,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions**\\n\\nFor users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to enter an empty guest namespace instead of remaining signed out. Remove the stale offline marker as part of expiration, while preserving it only for accounts explicitly created in offline mode.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6SI\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 260,\n      \"originalLine\": 268,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:57Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206001\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=179c0b6e-949a-450a-a389-f69cb4a8d5c4 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: When a user enables E2EE and then signs into a different account in the same browser, this global cache makes the new account reuse the previous account's DEK. Its runtime then encrypts and syncs new-account data without matching remote E2EE metadata, so other devices cannot unlock it; scope the settings/key cache by account namespace or clear it during sign-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts, line 268:\\n\\n<comment>When a user enables E2EE and then signs into a different account in the same browser, this global cache makes the new account reuse the previous account's DEK. Its runtime then encrypts and syncs new-account data without matching remote E2EE metadata, so other devices cannot unlock it; scope the settings/key cache by account namespace or clear it during sign-out.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,378 @@\\n+}\\n+\\n+export async function getLocalDatafnE2eeSettings() {\\n+  const raw = await clientStorage.get(ClientStorageKey.DATAFN_E2EE_SETTINGS);\\n+  if (!raw) return null;\\n+  return parse(raw) as NucleumDatafnE2eeSettings | null;\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6SW\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 186,\n      \"originalLine\": 181,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206015\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=192b913b-f3f8-4c32-bbaa-410bc61d68cf -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP1: Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts, line 181:\\n\\n<comment>Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -1,90 +1,236 @@\\n+      timezone\\n+    );\\n+    return {\\n+      $gte: range.start,\\n+      $lte: range.end\\n+    };\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Sb\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts\",\n      \"line\": 38,\n      \"originalLine\": 38,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206021\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=4a26eaff-5fd5-4573-ac72-296510e428ce -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=9a7e6eac-b146-4340-9e2b-54409b395acb -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: Custom agent: **Check System Design and Architectural Patterns**\\n\\nWhen existing UI state is stored under the old enum values, these renamed strings make it unreachable, and current consumers still reference the removed enum members. Preserve or migrate the old storage keys and update every consumer consistently.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts, line 38:\\n\\n<comment>When existing UI state is stored under the old enum values, these renamed strings make it unreachable, and current consumers still reference the removed enum members. Preserve or migrate the old storage keys and update every consumer consistently.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -35,11 +35,11 @@ export enum UIState {\\n   analyticsPage = \\\"analyticsPage\\\",\\n   manualLogQuickDuration = \\\"manualLogQuickDuration\\\",\\n-  manualLogRecentGoals = \\\"manualLogRecentGoals\\\",\\n+  manualLogRecentObjectives = \\\"manualLogRecentObjectives\\\",\\n   manualLogDurationMethod = \\\"manualLogDurationMethod\\\",\\n   recentFocusItems = \\\"recentFocusItems\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Se\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts\",\n      \"line\": 38,\n      \"originalLine\": 38,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206025\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=83008e5b-4f60-4d57-be94-8f17b53d344b -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: After callers move to the renamed members, existing users lose their persisted recent-goal and panel-selection state because the raw `uiState` keys changed. Migrate the old keys or read them as a fallback before switching to the new names.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts, line 38:\\n\\n<comment>After callers move to the renamed members, existing users lose their persisted recent-goal and panel-selection state because the raw `uiState` keys changed. Migrate the old keys or read them as a fallback before switching to the new names.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -35,11 +35,11 @@ export enum UIState {\\n   analyticsPage = \\\"analyticsPage\\\",\\n   manualLogQuickDuration = \\\"manualLogQuickDuration\\\",\\n-  manualLogRecentGoals = \\\"manualLogRecentGoals\\\",\\n+  manualLogRecentObjectives = \\\"manualLogRecentObjectives\\\",\\n   manualLogDurationMethod = \\\"manualLogDurationMethod\\\",\\n   recentFocusItems = \\\"recentFocusItems\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Sf\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 609,\n      \"originalLine\": 609,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206027\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=74adb245-1155-4663-8f26-acad72481976 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: Removing this `<span id=\\\"global-sync-status\\\">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById(\\\"global-sync-status\\\")?.getAttribute(\\\"data-syncstatus\\\")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync listener no longer reflects the current global sync status on initial load. Update `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal` (or remove it) to stop reading the deleted element, and confirm the span isn't needed for initial sync feedback.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte, line 609:\\n\\n<comment>Removing this `<span id=\\\"global-sync-status\\\">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById(\\\"global-sync-status\\\")?.getAttribute(\\\"data-syncstatus\\\")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync listener no longer reflects the current global sync status on initial load. Update `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal` (or remove it) to stop reading the deleted element, and confirm the span isn't needed for initial sync feedback.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -606,8 +606,6 @@\\n     <div id=\\\"toolbars\\\"></div>\\n-    <span id=\\\"global-sync-status\\\" data-syncstatus=\\\"\\\" data-syncfeedback=\\\"true\\\"\\n-    ></span>\\n   </ThemeLayer>\\n </div>\\n {#if import.meta.env.VITE_NATIVE_EMBED !== \\\"true\\\"}\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Sh\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 86,\n      \"originalLine\": 69,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206029\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=87316749-6b84-4f09-9f38-a848d86455fd -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offline storage, but this switch still accepts and persists `false`. Disable the switch while E2EE is enabled, or reject the change without persisting it.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so