ount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync listener no longer reflects the current global sync status on initial load. Update `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal` (or remove it) to stop reading the deleted element, and confirm the span isn't needed for initial sync feedback.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -606,8 +606,6 @@\\n     <div id=\\\"toolbars\\\"></div>\\n-    <span id=\\\"global-sync-status\\\" data-syncstatus=\\\"\\\" data-syncfeedback=\\\"true\\\"\\n-    ></span>\\n   </ThemeLayer>\\n </div>\\n {#if import.meta.env.VITE_NATIVE_EMBED !== \\\"true\\\"}\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Sh\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 86,\n      \"originalLine\": 69,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206029\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=87316749-6b84-4f09-9f38-a848d86455fd -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offline storage, but this switch still accepts and persists `false`. Disable the switch while E2EE is enabled, or reject the change without persisting it.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte, line 69:\\n\\n<comment>When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offline storage, but this switch still accepts and persists `false`. Disable the switch while E2EE is enabled, or reject the change without persisting it.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -20,6 +39,43 @@\\n+        appVersion: $appStore.version + \\\".\\\" + $appStore.build,\\n+        dapId: dapId ?? undefined,\\n+        isOffline: $context.isInOfflineMode,\\n+        isOfflinabilityEnabled: nextValue\\n+      });\\n+    } catch {\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6TI\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 30,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206079\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=3305c83a-6926-4b7c-a3d0-8b2dda285386 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: This import makes `AccessMode.POP` passed to `ResourceResolver` a different enum type from its `accessMode` prop, causing the app type check to fail. Keep the legacy import until `ResourceResolver` migrates too, or migrate both together.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte, line 30:\\n\\n<comment>This import makes `AccessMode.POP` passed to `ResourceResolver` a different enum type from its `accessMode` prop, causing the app type check to fail. Keep the legacy import until `ResourceResolver` migrates too, or migrate both together.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -27,11 +27,12 @@\\n   import Trail from \\\"../trail/Trail.svelte\\\";\\n   import type { IAction } from \\\"@21n/types/action.type\\\";\\n-  import { AccessMode } from \\\"@21n/components/flux/resourceStores/resource.type\\\";\\n+  import { AccessMode } from \\\"@21n/data/datafn/resource.type\\\";\\n   import type { IRecordId } from \\\"@21n/types/data.type\\\";\\n   import ResourceResolver from \\\"../paint/ResourceResolver.svelte\\\";\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6TM\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/account.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 946,\n      \"originalLine\": 883,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206083\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=c6f81909-7a2d-4fa6-8b8c-2aab3b248bb0 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} -->\\nP2: `checkIfSessionExpired` removed the offline short-circuit that previously returned `false` whenever an offline session existed without an AuthFn token. A LOCAL/offline-only user (no AuthFn session) now goes through `resolveAuthSession()`, which can report the missing session as expired and kick them back to sign-in. Preserve the offline-only early return before calling `resolveAuthSession`.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/account.store.ts, line 882:\\n\\n<comment>`checkIfSessionExpired` removed the offline short-circuit that previously returned `false` whenever an offline session existed without an AuthFn token. A LOCAL/offline-only user (no AuthFn session) now goes through `resolveAuthSession()`, which can report the missing session as expired and kick them back to sign-in. Preserve the offline-only early return before calling `resolveAuthSession`.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -874,28 +879,8 @@ class AccountStore extends ObservableStore<UserAccount> {\\n-      logger.error({ at: \\\"checkIfSessionExpired.authfn\\\", error });\\n-      return true;\\n-    }\\n+    const resolution = await resolveAuthSession();\\n+    return resolution.status === \\\"expired\\\";\\n   }\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const offlineSessionId = await clientStorage.get(\\n      ClientStorageKey.OFFLINE_SESSION_ID\\n    );\\n    const authFnToken = shouldUseAuthFnBearerSession()\\n      ? await clientStorage.get(ClientStorageKey.AUTHFN_TOKEN)\\n …12680 tokens truncated…hese consumers to subscribe directly.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlS86\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/cache/InMemoryCache.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 37,\n      \"originalLine\": 31,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891015251\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the collection cache mounted in host apps**\\n\\nIn normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron flows, this replacement mounts only the global calendar cache and creates signals for total resource counts and node subtypes. The previous `CollectionCache` action was removed, and repo-wide search shows it is now mounted only by the clipper, leaving no host-app producer for `collection-item-counts` or `typed-collection-cache`; consequently collection item badges and typed-collection avatars remain empty. Retain the shared collection cache until equivalent DataFn relation signals populate those keys.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L9-L10](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/9aadca2ea993fabb62fb72a655327ed3fb14d51c/AGENTS.md#L9-L10)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlcuC\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/datafn.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 900,\n      \"originalLine\": 855,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075824\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore E2EE after a failed disable attempt**\\n\\nIf writing the disabled metadata or `cloneUpAllDatafnData()` fails, this has already removed E2EE from the live client. The catch restores the old metadata and calls `initializeNucleumDatafn()`, but the runtime key still contains the same `keyRef`, so initialization returns the existing runtime without reinstalling its provider. Subsequent sync writes can therefore remain unencrypted even though both local and remote settings still report E2EE enabled; explicitly restore the provider/context before propagating the failure.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/91a40ab57f575d1eed347dcb7a09f9555b21f510/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlcuF\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 92,\n      \"originalLine\": 88,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075826\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow cached Nucleum sessions to use their offline clone**\\n\\nWhen a Nucleum cloud user with offlinability enabled launches during a network outage or manual offline mode, `resolveAuthSession()` deliberately returns `cached-cloud`, but this branch unconditionally sends them to access denied without consulting any cached entitlement. Unlike the prior gate, which only denied a known non-Nucleum plan, this locks every entitled Nucleum user out of the local clone whenever the account service cannot be reached.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/91a40ab57f575d1eed347dcb7a09f9555b21f510/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlcuK\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 1233,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075834\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve PointLog rows that predate session IDs**\\n\\nFor legacy Pointron `PointLog` rows created before sessions were attached, `sessionId` is absent—the retained legacy `FocusLog` type still declares it optional—so this conversion silently drops otherwise valid `start`, `totalFocus`, and `totalBreak` history. Recovery then records a successful decision and suppresses future prompts because these pre-import omissions are not reported as skipped rows. The fresh evidence after the prior conversion is this explicit rejection of every row lacking `sessionId`; generate a deterministic legacy session reference or otherwise preserve those analytics rows.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/91a40ab57f575d1eed347dcb7a09f9555b21f510/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRp\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 178,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122427\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the cached plan when entitlement refresh fails**\\n\\nWhen an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the plan endpoint is temporarily unavailable, the account update immediately above has already cleared the cached plan and this condition treats the missing response as a failed entitlement. Entitled Nucleum users are consequently redirected to access denied despite the newly persisted `USER_PLAN`; fall back to that validated cached plan on refresh failures while continuing to deny a known non-Nucleum plan.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRq\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/record/recent.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 128,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table**\\n\\nFor Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \\\"search\\\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compatibility mapping already used elsewhere.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRr\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"originalLine\": 66,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122431\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode**\\n\\nWhen a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude `sync-direct` here or make the flow enable offlinability before setup.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlkRs\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 28,\n      \"originalLine\": 28,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122432\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Recompute network state after reconnecting**\\n\\nIf Sync Settings is mounted while the browser is offline and then the connection returns, `isNetworkInducedOfflineMode` remains the mount-time value `true`. Although `BaseLayer` updates `$context.isInOfflineMode` to false, this new toggle therefore stays disabled until the settings component is remounted, preventing the user from changing offline availability after reconnecting. Derive this value from reactive connectivity state rather than the fixed `navigator.onLine` snapshot.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dloMk\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1241,\n      \"originalLine\": 1235,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:28:48Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146946\",\n          \"body\": \"Sessionless `PointLog` rows now receive a `sessionId`, but the import payload never creates the corresponding `session`. The remote schema enforces this required foreign key, and legacy streak rows concretely omit `sessionId`, so their recovery can fail instead of preserving them.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Preserve sessionless PointLog rows without orphaned references\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts:1233-1235` — invents a session foreign key without adding that session resource.\\n- `shared/data/datafn/schema.datafn.ts:646-652` — declares `sessionLog.sessionId` as the required relation to `session`.\\n- `services/account/src/db/generated/datafn/datafn-schema.drizzle.ts:419` — enforces the composite foreign key remotely.\\n- `server/surreal-archive/pointron/analytics/streak/insertEmpty.surql:4` — creates legacy PointLog records without session IDs.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Import these records with valid matching session resources, or handle them through an explicit supported representation that cannot violate the remote relation.\\n- Add a migration fixture for a PointLog without `sessionId` that verifies the complete import payload.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dluiN\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1256,\n      \"originalLine\": 1256,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:43:01Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:43:02Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891185888\",\n          \"body\": \"## Comparison between inconvertible types\\n\\n<p>Variable 'startUnix' cannot be of type undefined, but it is compared to <a class=\\\"Link\\\" href=\\\"/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts#L1256-L1256\\\">'undefined'</a> of type undefined.</p>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dluiP\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1262,\n      \"originalLine\": 1262,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:43:01Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:43:02Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891185892\",\n          \"body\": \"## Comparison between inconvertible types\\n\\n<p>Variable 'endUnix' cannot be of type undefined, but it is compared to <a class=\\\"Link\\\" href=\\\"/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts#L1262-L1262\\\">'undefined'</a> of type undefined.</p>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlzA1\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 329,\n      \"originalLine\": 329,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213265\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Confirm native backup delivery before suppressing recovery**\\n\\nIn an embedded iOS/macOS recovery flow, `downloadLegacyLocalBackup()` starts the asynchronous `fileStore.downloadFromBlob()` upload/handoff without awaiting or validating it, and this branch immediately saves `download_backup_continue`. If the upload fails or returns no URL, the UI still reports success and permanently suppresses the startup recovery prompt even though the user received no backup; make the helper report delivery success and await it before saving the decision.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlzA3\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/account.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 878,\n      \"originalLine\": 878,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213268\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject failed DataFn file metadata mutations**\\n\\nWhen an S3 upload succeeds but the following DataFn mutation resolves with `{ ok: false }`, this code ignores the result and returns `[file]` as though persistence succeeded. Callers such as `MediaGrid.uploadToS3()` then retain the returned file reference even though no file record exists, producing broken attachments; inspect the mutation result and propagate its error before returning success.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlzA4\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\",\n      \"line\": 435,\n      \"originalLine\": 435,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213269\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore automatic timezone-change capture**\\n\\nWhen a Pointron or Nucleum user travels and later focuses the app, `onAppear()` no longer detects or records the browser timezone change; the former `refreshTimeZone()` call was removed, and repo-wide search finds no remaining automatic caller of `userPreferences.setTimeZone()`. Consequently DataFn's temporal history remains stale, so calendar boundaries and historical analytics continue using the previous zone unless the user manually changes settings.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dlzA6\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/stores/account.store.ts\",\n      \"line\": 946,\n      \"originalLine\": 946,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213274\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unavailable sessions in extension checks**\\n\\nWhen AuthFn returns `unavailable` and the stored session is not eligible for cached-cloud use—for example, an extension has a bearer token but no cached `USER_INFO`, or offlinability is disabled—this returns `false`. `SheetBaseLayer.performSessionExpiryCheck()` and `ExtensionBaseLayer.checkIfSessionExpired()` interpret that as an active session and proceed to initialize authenticated extension data instead of showing the login/service error, so only authenticated, cached-cloud, or offline-only resolutions should be considered usable here.\\n\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L86-L86](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/AGENTS.md#L86-L86)\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dl0yL\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1248,\n      \"originalLine\": 1248,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:56:04Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-31T01:56:05Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891224029\",\n          \"body\": \"The exact sessionless rows cited by the original finding are created with `goalId: \\\"PointGoal:Empty\\\"`, but no matching goal exists. This converts that sentinel to `objective:Empty`, and the generated remote schema enforces `sessionLog.objectiveId` as a foreign key, so creating the synthetic session only moves the import failure to this relation. Drop the sentinel objective reference or create a matching supported resource, and add the exact streak-row fixture to verify the complete payload.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reviewsAfterCommit\": [],\n  \"issueCommentsAfterCommit\": [],\n  \"inlineCommentsAfterCommit\": []\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1788141494239,"completed_at_ms":1788141502159}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T01:58:22.166Z","ordinal":7222,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a05589-fed6-7ed1-bbe4-411d31688ae2","call_id":"call_dZg32bHhrUztETdMg59TdHRT","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 8.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 21044)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"1c8719\",\"wall_time_seconds\":7.919576417,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":22680,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 22680)\\nTotal output lines: 930\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"snapshotDir\\\": \\\"/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot.daFT68\\\",\\n  \\\"commitTime\\\": \\\"2026-08-31T07:11:23+05:30\\\",\\n  \\\"pr\\\": {\\n    \\\"baseRefName\\\": \\\"dev\\\",\\n    \\\"headRefName\\\": \\\"codex/tidy-442-04-client-runtime-auth\\\",\\n    \\\"headRefOid\\\": \\\"ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b\\\",\\n    \\\"mergeStateStatus\\\": \\\"UNSTABLE\\\",\\n    \\\"mergeable\\\": \\\"MERGEABLE\\\",\\n    \\\"number\\\": 570,\\n    \\\"state\\\": \\\"OPEN\\\",\\n    \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-31T01:56:05Z\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"counts\\\": {\\n    \\\"reviewThreads\\\": 126,\\n    \\\"unresolvedThreads\\\": 53,\\n    \\\"unresolvedCurrentThreads\\\": 38,\\n    \\\"reviews\\\": 44,\\n    \\\"issueComments\\\": 8,\\n    \\\"inlineComments\\\": 140,\\n    \\\"threadsWithOver100Comments\\\": 0\\n  },\\n  \\\"unresolvedThreads\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY5j3\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 554,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 430,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201424\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep Flux initialized until all product stores migrate**\\\\n\\\\nIn the normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron app flow, this now initializes only DataFn, while numerous unchanged product stores still call the exported legacy `flux` instance—for example, `ResourceStore.create()` invokes `flux.mutation()` and node/history code invokes `flux.selectMany()`. That export remains a null cast until `initFlux()` runs, and repo-wide search shows initialization now occurs only in sheet and extension flows, so ordinary create, edit, and select interactions fail at runtime even though DataFn startup succeeds. Keep the compatibility runtime initialized or migrate every remaining consumer in the same change.\\\\n\\\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L80-L83](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L80-L83)\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY5j4\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/stores/account.store.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 420,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 370,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201425\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clear DataFn data before destroying the runtime**\\\\n\\\\nWhen AuthFn account deletion succeeds, `signOut()` first calls `destroyNucleumDatafn()`, which clears `runtimeStore`; the following `clearDatafnLocalData()` immediately returns because there is no `runtime?.storage`. Consequently, deleting an account leaves its IndexedDB cache and user data on the device. Clear the active storage before signing out, or retain the storage handle through deletion.\\\\n\\\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY5j5\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/components/account/auth.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 238,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 275,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"chatgpt-codex-connector\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions**\\\\n\\\\nFor users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to enter an empty guest namespace instead of remaining signed out. Remove the stale offline marker as part of expiration, while preserving it only for accounts explicitly created in offline mode.\\\\n\\\\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6SI\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 260,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 268,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:53:57Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206001\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=179c0b6e-949a-450a-a389-f69cb4a8d5c4 -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP1: When a user enables E2EE and then signs into a different account in the same browser, this global cache makes the new account reuse the previous account's DEK. Its runtime then encrypts and syncs new-account data without matching remote E2EE metadata, so other devices cannot unlock it; scope the settings/key cache by account namespace or clear it during sign-out.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts, line 268:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When a user enables E2EE and then signs into a different account in the same browser, this global cache makes the new account reuse the previous account's DEK. Its runtime then encrypts and syncs new-account data without matching remote E2EE metadata, so other devices cannot unlock it; scope the settings/key cache by account namespace or clear it during sign-out.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -0,0 +1,378 @@\\\\n+}\\\\n+\\\\n+export async function getLocalDatafnE2eeSettings() {\\\\n+  const raw = await clientStorage.get(ClientStorageKey.DATAFN_E2EE_SETTINGS);\\\\n+  if (!raw) return null;\\\\n+  return parse(raw) as NucleumDatafnE2eeSettings | null;\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6SW\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 186,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 181,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206015\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=192b913b-f3f8-4c32-bbaa-410bc61d68cf -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":10} -->\\\\nP1: Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts, line 181:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -1,90 +1,236 @@\\\\n+      timezone\\\\n+    );\\\\n+    return {\\\\n+      $gte: range.start,\\\\n+      $lte: range.end\\\\n+    };\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Sb\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 38,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 38,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206021\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=4a26eaff-5fd5-4573-ac72-296510e428ce -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=9a7e6eac-b146-4340-9e2b-54409b395acb -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP1: Custom agent: **Check System Design and Architectural Patterns**\\\\n\\\\nWhen existing UI state is stored under the old enum values, these renamed strings make it unreachable, and current consumers still reference the removed enum members. Preserve or migrate the old storage keys and update every consumer consistently.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts, line 38:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>When existing UI state is stored under the old enum values, these renamed strings make it unreachable, and current consumers still reference the removed enum members. Preserve or migrate the old storage keys and update every consumer consistently.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -35,11 +35,11 @@ export enum UIState {\\\\n   analyticsPage = \\\\\\\"analyticsPage\\\\\\\",\\\\n   manualLogQuickDuration = \\\\\\\"manualLogQuickDuration\\\\\\\",\\\\n-  manualLogRecentGoals = \\\\\\\"manualLogRecentGoals\\\\\\\",\\\\n+  manualLogRecentObjectives = \\\\\\\"manualLogRecentObjectives\\\\\\\",\\\\n   manualLogDurationMethod = \\\\\\\"manualLogDurationMethod\\\\\\\",\\\\n   recentFocusItems = \\\\\\\"recentFocusItems\\\\\\\",\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Se\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 38,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 38,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206025\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=83008e5b-4f60-4d57-be94-8f17b53d344b -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP2: After callers move to the renamed members, existing users lose their persisted recent-goal and panel-selection state because the raw `uiState` keys changed. Migrate the old keys or read them as a fallback before switching to the new names.\\\\n\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts, line 38:\\\\n\\\\n<comment>After callers move to the renamed members, existing users lose their persisted recent-goal and panel-selection state because the raw `uiState` keys changed. Migrate the old keys or read them as a fallback before switching to the new names.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -35,11 +35,11 @@ export enum UIState {\\\\n   analyticsPage = \\\\\\\"analyticsPage\\\\\\\",\\\\n   manualLogQuickDuration = \\\\\\\"manualLogQuickDuration\\\\\\\",\\\\n-  manualLogRecentGoals = \\\\\\\"manualLogRecentGoals\\\\\\\",\\\\n+  manualLogRecentObjec