Removing this `<span id=\\\\\\\"global-sync-status\\\\\\\">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById(\\\\\\\"global-sync-status\\\\\\\")?.getAttribute(\\\\\\\"data-syncstatus\\\\\\\")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync listener no longer reflects the current global sync status on initial load. Update `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal` (or remove it) to stop reading the deleted element, and confirm the span isn't needed for initial sync feedback.</comment>\\\\n\\\\n<file context>\\\\n@@ -606,8 +606,6 @@\\\\n     <div id=\\\\\\\"toolbars\\\\\\\"></div>\\\\n-    <span id=\\\\\\\"global-sync-status\\\\\\\" data-syncstatus=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" data-syncfeedback=\\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\"\\\\n-    ></span>\\\\n   </ThemeLayer>\\\\n </div>\\\\n {#if import.meta.env.VITE_NATIVE_EMBED !== \\\\\\\"true\\\\\\\"}\\\\n</file context>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"PRRT_kwDOO5p-Xs6dY6Sh\\\",\\n      \\\"isOutdated\\\": false,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 86,\\n      \\\"originalLine\\\": 69,\\n      \\\"comments\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"author\\\": \\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\",\\n          \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\\\",\\n          \\\"updatedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T09:54:00Z\\\",\\n          \\\"outdated\\\": false,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206029\\\",\\n          \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- cubic:v=87316749-6b84-4f09-9f38-a848d86455fd -->\\\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 -->\\\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} -->\\\\nP2: When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offli