{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:35:24.556Z","ordinal":8133,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a053e7-239f-7703-8a5b-d9d8ac22d6de","turn_id":"01a055a0-b7e6-7830-822b-e49301a714ef","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-80fb79fd-2765-4f9e-a2ab-2df2d69c0544","process_id":"74997","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cutoff=$(date -u -r \"$(git show -s --format=%ct fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311)\" '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'); printf 'cutoff %s\\n' \"$cutoff\"; jq -r --arg cutoff \"$cutoff\" '.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | select($c.createdAt >= $cutoff) | [(.path // $c.path // \"\"), (.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0 | tostring), $c.createdAt, ($c.author.login // \"\"), ($c.commit.oid // \"\"), ($c.outdated | tostring), ($c.url // \"\"), ($c.body | gsub(\"[\\r\\n]+\"; \" \"))] | @tsv' /tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-fa3b4457.UGIQWY/threads.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-570-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cutoff=$(date -u -r \"$(git show -s --format=%ct fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311)\" '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'); printf 'cutoff %s\\n' \"$cutoff\"; jq -r --arg cutoff \"$cutoff\" '.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | select($c.createdAt >= $cutoff) | [(.path // $c.path // \"\"), (.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0 | tostring), $c.createdAt, ($c.author.login // \"\"), ($c.commit.oid // \"\"), ($c.outdated | tostring), ($c.url // \"\"), ($c.body | gsub(\"[\\r\\n]+\"; \" \"))] | @tsv' /tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-fa3b4457.UGIQWY/threads.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"cutoff 2026-08-31T02:22:33Z\nclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t670\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321872\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map goal collection searches to objective** When “Add item to collection” is used for a Pointron goal collection or a goal-typed Nucleum collection, `Collection.svelte` passes the legacy `goal` resource here, but the DataFn schema exposes that resource as `objective`. Forwarding `goal` to `datafn.search()` makes non-empty searches fail or return no goals, even though the blank-query recents path has a compatibility mapping; translate `goal` to `objective` before searching. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\nclient/stores/app.store.ts\t207\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321878\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the legacy goal route in the mobile menu gate** On portrait layouts, breadcrumb navigation still calls `gotoResource()` with legacy resource IDs and therefore produces paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers are migrated. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\nclient/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts\t78\t2026-08-31T02:30:26Z\tpullfrog\tfa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891328228\tThis map survives DataFn namespace/account changes, so an unacknowledged write from account A is reapplied over account B's signal state. Because setters such as `setAppearance()` merge from the displayed store, the stale value can then be persisted into B; clear or namespace pending entries whenever the DataFn context changes. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Keep optimistic user preferences account-scoped ## Affected sites - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts:78` — stores pending entries in one process-global map. - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts:109-115` — reapplies every unmatched pending entry after any namespace's signal update. - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts:138-142` — derives a persisted nested value from the potentially overlaid store. - `client/stores/account.store.ts:233` — destroys DataFn on sign-out without resetting this pending state. ## Required outcome - Pending user-preference entries must never be applied outside the DataFn namespace that created them. - Preserve per-mutation rollback behavior and cover a namespace switch while a preference write remains unacknowledged. ```` </details>\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t603\t2026-08-31T02:33:49Z\tcoderabbitai\tfa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891339508\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_ <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary> 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable repository conventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -maxdepth 3 -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- changed hunk ---' sed -n '540,630p' client/stores/datafn.store.ts printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct definitions and calls ---' rg -n -C 4 'writeRemoteDatafnE2eeSettings|clearDatafnE2eeRecovery|recoveryRequired|initializeNucleumDatafn|datafn.*(set|put|update)|remote.*(revision|version)' client shared ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of output: 33605 --- 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e printf '%s\\\\n' '--- client conventions ---' cat /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nc