cture primarily relies on its core database adapter contract (superfunctions/db) and Drizzle-based schemas [6][7]. 2. There is no publicly documented kv.set API in `@datafn/client` that handles explicit revision-based conditional writes (e.g., compare-and-swap or version-checking) as a primary feature. 3. If you are encountering revision conflicts in DataFn, these are typically managed at the database transaction layer—DataFn generates internal tables (prefixed with datafn_*) to track changes and synchronization state [6]. 4. Conflicts in DataFn are generally resolved through the framework's internal synchronization and transaction management rather than via manual client-side revision checks on a simple key-value store [6][7]. For specific implementation details or to confirm the status of experimental APIs, you should consult the latest source code within the 21nCo/super-functions repository, specifically under the datafn/core/src/kv.ts module, which manages the KV logic [3]. Citations: - 1: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions - 2: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/README.md - 3: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/038d6a5a253bc2bce61eed3358dd9fd37e547b30 - 4: https://registry.npmjs.org/@vercel/kv - 5: https://docs.deno.com/deploy/kv/operations/ - 6: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/7847ad5daabdda109384466908a9086eac097a00 - 7: GitHub issue 90 in 21nCo/super-functions (link omitted to avoid creating a cross-reference) --- 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e tmpdir=\"$(mktemp -d)\" trap 'rm -rf \"$tmpdir\"' EXIT url='https://registry.npmjs.org/@datafn/client/-/client-0.1.0.tgz' curl -fsSL \"$url\" -o \"$tmpdir/client.tgz\" tar -xzf \"$tmpdir/client.tgz\" -C \"$tmpdir\" printf '%s\\\\n' '--- package contents ---' find \"$tmpdir/package\" -maxdepth 3 -type f -print | sort printf '%s\\\\n' '--- KV implementation and types ---' rg -n -C 8 'class .*Kv|kv\\\\.|set\\\\(|get\\\\(|merge\\\\(|revision|conflict|versio