onventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -maxdepth 3 -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- changed hunk ---' sed -n '540,630p' client/stores/datafn.store.ts printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct definitions and calls ---' rg -n -C 4 'writeRemoteDatafnE2eeSettings|clearDatafnE2eeRecovery|recoveryRequired|initializeNucleumDatafn|datafn.*(set|put|update)|remote.*(revision|version)' client shared ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of output: 33605 --- 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e printf '%s\\\\n' '--- client conventions ---' cat /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00/conventions/client.md printf '%s\\\\n' '--- repository-wide conventions ---' cat /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00/conventions/repo-wide.md printf '%s\\\\n' '--- remote settings helpers and imports ---' sed -n '1,90p' client/stores/datafn.store.ts sed -n '420,525p' client/stores/datafn.store.ts printf '%s\\\\n' '--- E2EE settings type and constructors ---' sed -n '1,80p' client/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts sed -n '330,390p' client/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts printf '%s\\\\n' '--- DataFn metadata API declarations/usages ---' rg -n -C 5 'metadataClient|createDatafnMetadata|DatafnMetadata|kv\\\\.(get|set)|class .*Metadata|interface .*Metadata' --glob '*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}' . ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of output: 23518 --- 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e printf '%s\\\\n' '--- dependency versions and repository metadata ---' rg -n '\"`@datafn/client`\"|datafn/client|datafn' package.json pnpm-lock.yaml package-lock.json yarn.lock bun.lockb 2>/dev/null || true printf '%s\\\\n' '--- available dependency/source files ---' git ls-files | rg '(^|/)(package.json|.*lock|datafn|DataFn|data-fn)' | head -80 printf '%s\\\\n' '--- all KV contract references in tracked source ---' rg -n -C 6 'kv\\\\.(get|set)|type .*Kv|interface .*Kv|class .*Kv|conditional|revision|conflict|compare.?and|if.?match' --glob '*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,md}' . | head -300 ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of output: 24816 --- 🌐 Web query: `@datafn/client 0.1.0 kv.set get DataFn KV API conditional write revision conflict` 💡 Result: The `@datafn/client` package is part of the DataFn framework within the 21nCo super-functions ecosystem [1][2]. While the documentation mentions a built-in KV (key-value) utility [3], it does not expose a public, standalone `@datafn/client` KV API equivalent to the standard patterns found in services like Deno KV or Vercel KV [4][5]. Regarding your query on revision conflicts and conditional writes in DataFn KV: 1. DataFn architecture primarily relies on its core database adapter contract (superfunctions/db) and Drizzle-based schemas [6][7]. 2. There is no publicly documented kv.set API in `@datafn/client` that handles explicit revision-based conditional writes (e.g., compare-and-swap or version-checking) as a primary feature. 3. If you are encountering revision conflicts in DataFn, these are typically managed at the database transaction layer—DataFn generates internal tables (prefixed with datafn_*) to track changes and synchronization state [6]. 4. Conflicts in DataFn are generally resolved through the framework's internal synchronization and transaction management rather than via manual client-side revision checks on a simple key-value store [6][7]. For specific implementation details or to confirm the status of experimental APIs, you should consult the latest source code within the 21nCo/super-functions repository, specifically under the datafn/core/src/kv.ts module, which manages the KV logic [3]. Citations: - 1: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions - 2: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/README.md - 3: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/038d6a5a253bc2bce61eed3358dd9fd37e547b30 - 4: https://registry.npmjs.org/@vercel/kv - 5: https://docs.deno.com/deploy/kv/operations/ - 6: https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/7847ad5daabdda109384466