>Prompt for AI agent\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t375\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827045\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve sync-direct writes across offline transitions** When a cloud user has disabled offlinability, a manual or network outage still takes this unconditional branch and opens a new, initially empty local-only database. Edits made there cannot clone up because the runtime is local-only; on reconnect, initialization returns to `sync-direct` and deletes that retired database, silently discarding those edits. Keep sync-direct read-only while offline, prevent this transition, or upload the temporary clone bef\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t537\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210778\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Abort startup when remote E2EE settings cannot be read** When an E2EE-enabled account starts on a new device without cached local settings and this metadata request fails transiently, converting the failure to `null` makes `resolveDatafnE2eeConfig()` treat encryption as disabled. Initialization then opens normal sync with `e2ee: null`, so the user cannot decrypt existing records and subsequent writes may be uploaded without the account's encryption. Preserve the error and stop startup until the remote encry\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t912\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075824\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore E2EE after a failed disable attempt** If writing the disabled metadata or `cloneUpAllDatafnData()` fails, this has already removed E2EE from the live client. The catch restores