le=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode** When a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude `sync-direct` here or make the flow enable offlinability before setup. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\nclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t120\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827057\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid clone-up for local-only restores** When an offline-only account or a cloud account currently in offline mode restores a backup, this always requests `triggerCloneUp` even though the active runtime has no remote transport. The import can therefore fail after writing local rows, leaving the UI reporting failure with a partially restored database; the legacy recovery path already avoids this by enabling clone-up only when `runtime.mode === \"sync\"`. Apply the same mode check here. AGENTS.md reference: [AG\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t28\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122432\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Recompute network state after reconnecting** If Sync Settings is mounted while the browser is offline and then the connection returns, `isNetworkInducedOfflineMode` remains the mount-time value `true`. Although `BaseLayer` updates `$context.isInOfflineMode` to false, this new toggle therefore stays disabled until the settings component is remounted, preventing the user from changing offline availability after reconnecting. Derive this value from reactive connectivity state rather than the fixed `navigator.o\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t79\t2026-08-30T22:59:12Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890782302\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Delete the local clone when disabling offlinability** When a sync user turns off “Keep data available offline,” this initialization only closes the current adapter and switches to `sync-direct`; neither this handler nor the runtime teardown deletes or clears the retired IndexedDB database. The device therefore retains the user's complete local clone indefinitely despite the setting promising that no local copy is kept; after pending changes are flushed, delete the old namespace database as part of the trans\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t86\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206029\t<!-- cubic:v=87316749-6b84-4f09-9f38-a848d86455fd --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P2: When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offline storage, but this switch still accepts and persists `false`. Disable the switch while E2EE is enabled, or reject the change without persisting it. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte, line 69: <comment>When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always \nclient/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\t186\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206015\t<!-- cubic:v=192b913b-f3f8-4c32-bbaa-410bc61d68cf --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} --> P1: Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/timezone/tz.stor\nclient/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\t298\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269353\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply the historical timezone correction instead of a round trip** When a Pointron user has timezone-change records, `AnalyticsCardView` and `AnalyticsChartStandalone` depend on this method to normalize historical session timestamps. Resolving date parts in a timezone and immediately resolving those same parts back in the same timezone returns the original instant, so the correction is effectively a no-op and sessions can be grouped or filtered into the wrong day after travel; the conversion needs to accoun\nclient/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts\t129\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265052\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore writable updates for preference bindings** Svelte compiles assignments and bindings such as those in `SizeFactorSetting`, `AppearanceSettings`, `DateTimeSettings`, and `CmdResults` into calls to `userPreferences.set(...)`, but this replacement exposes only `subscribe`, `get`, and `modify`. When users change sizing, popup blur, time scales, day-start values, or recent commands, the generated handler therefore fails instead of updating and persisting the preference; restore a persistence-aware `set` m\nclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t48\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827049\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore the Nucleum entitlement gate after authentication** For cloud users opening the Nucleum product, this replacement admits every successful session without the prior `account.ping()` and `PlanType.NUCLEUS` check. A repo-wide search finds no remaining navigation to `/error/access-denied`, and AuthFn session resolution does not populate or enforce the account plan, so users with only a Memotron or Pointron entitlement can enter the combined Nucleum UI. Restore the product-specific entitlement check afte\nclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t92\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075826\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow cached Nucleum sessions to use their offline clone** When a Nucleum cloud user with offlinability enabled launches during a network outage or manual offline mode, `resolveAuthSession()` deliberately returns `cached-cloud`, but this branch unconditionally sends them to access denied without consulting any cached entitlement. Unlike the prior gate, which only denied a known non-Nucleum plan, this locks every entitled Nucleum user out of the local clone whenever the account service cannot be reached. AGE\nclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t178\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122427\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the cached plan when entitlement refresh fails** When an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the plan endpoint is temporarily unavailable, the account update immediately above has already cleared the cached plan and this condition treats the missing response as a failed entitlement. Entitled Nucleum users are consequently redirected to access denied despite the newly persisted `USER_PLAN`; fall back to that validated cached plan on refresh failures while\nclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t461\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269351\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve manual offline mode across connectivity events** When a user has explicitly enabled offline mode and the browser reconnects, this handler derives `isOffline` solely from `navigator.onLine`, overwrites the stored-mode state, and switches DataFn back to sync. The reconnect can therefore upload locally queued changes despite the user's offline-mode selection; combine network state with `ClientStorageKey.OFFLINE_MODE` before updating the runtime, and invoke the same runtime update when the manual toggl\nclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t609\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206027\t<!-- cubic:v=74adb245-1155-4663-8f26-acad72481976 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P2: Removing this `<span id=\"global-sync-status\">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById(\"global-sync-status\")?.getAttribute(\"data-syncstatus\")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync list\nclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t176\t2026-08-30T23:51:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t9aadca2ea9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890895070\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bridge legacy Flux mutations into DataFn** When unchanged flows such as `nodeStore.create()` or `taskStore.create()` run, `ResourceStore` writes to the Dexie-backed legacy `flux`, not `datafn`. This call starts that independent runtime after DataFn, but nothing imports subsequent Flux mutations; additionally, `SyncLayer.svelte` now invokes only `pullDatafnNow()`, and repo-wide search finds no remaining `flux.sync()` call. Thus newly created or edited records can remain outside DataFn search/cache and never \nclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t329\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213265\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Confirm native backup delivery before suppressing recovery** In an embedded iOS/macOS recovery flow, `downloadLegacyLocalBackup()` starts the asynchronous `fileStore.downloadFromBlob()` upload/handoff without awaiting or validating it, and this branch immediately saves `download_backup_continue`. If the upload fails or returns no URL, the UI still reports success and permanently suppresses the startup recovery prompt even though the user received no backup; make the helper report delivery success and await \nclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t439\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213269\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore automatic timezone-change capture** When a Pointron or Nucleum user travels and later focuses the app, `onAppear()` no longer detects or records the browser timezone change; the former `refreshTimeZone()` call was removed, and repo-wide search finds no remaining automatic caller of `userPreferences.setTimeZone()`. Consequently DataFn's temporal history remains stale, so calendar boundaries and historical analytics continue using the previous zone unless the user manually changes settings. AGENTS.md \nclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t576\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201424\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep Flux initialized until all product stores migrate** In the normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron app flow, this now initializes only DataFn, while numerous unchanged product stores still call the exported legacy `flux` instance—for example, `ResourceStore.create()` invokes `flux.mutation()` and node/history code invokes `flux.selectMany()`. That export remains a null cast until `initFlux()` runs, and repo-wide search shows initialization now occurs only in sheet and extension flows, so ordinary create\nclient/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte\t30\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206079\t<!-- cubic:v=3305c83a-6926-4b7c-a3d0-8b2dda285386 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P2: This import makes `AccessMode.POP` passed to `ResourceResolver` a different enum type from its `accessMode` prop, causing the app type check to fail. Keep the legacy import until `ResourceResolver` migrates too, or migrate both together. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte, line 30: <comment>This import\nclient/layout/layers/cache/InMemoryCache.svelte\t37\t2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891015251\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the collection cache mounted in host apps** In normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron flows, this replacement mounts only the global calendar cache and creates signals for total resource counts and node subtypes. The previous `CollectionCache` action was removed, and repo-wide search shows it is now mounted only by the clipper, leaving no host-app producer for `collection-item-counts` or `typed-collection-cache`; consequently collection item badges and typed-collection avatars remain empty. Retain the \nclient/layout/layers/cache/cache.store.ts\t18\t2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891015247\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep dispatching cache update events** When DataFn resource-count or node-subtype signals emit after a consumer has mounted, `cache.replace()` now updates only the internal store. Consumers such as `ResourceSwitcherItem` and `LibrarySubTypeSwitcher` read via `cache.retrieve()` rather than subscribing to the store, and rely exclusively on `ComponentBaseLayer`'s `cacheUpdate` event to refresh, so their displayed counts remain at the initial value after creates, deletes, archives, or syncs. Preserve the event \nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t164\t2026-08-31T00:20:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963089\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Convert legacy timezone rows during recovery** For migrated Pointron or Nucleum users with records in the legacy `tz` store, this map has no timezone target, so `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"tz\")` returns undefined and recovery silently skips the history even though detection recognizes `tz` as a legacy resource store. The replacement timezone store reads only `datafn.temporal.listTimezoneChanges()`, leaving historical timezone corrections unavailable and causing analytics around earlier timezone changes to \nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t173\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827046\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Translate PointLog fields before importing** For old Pointron databases containing `PointLog`, mapping the store directly to `sessionLog` is insufficient: historical rows use fields such as `totalFocus`, `totalBreak`, `start`, and `goalId`, while the DataFn schema requires modern fields including `startUnix`, `endUnix`, and `sessionId`. The current transform only renames `goalId`, so filtering against the schema drops the focus metrics and the required-field failures cause these rows to be skipped, preventi\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t396\t2026-08-29T10:00:24Z\tpullfrog\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886218145\tLegacy Dexie databases are named `${userOrDapId}-1`, but this accepts every `*-1` database while [`detectLegacyLocalData()`](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts#L201-L235) enumerates the whole browser. On a shared device, account B can therefore import account A's records into B's DataFn namespace; discovery and import need to be scoped to the active identity. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Scope legacy recovery to the signed-in identity ## Affected sites - `client/persistence/l\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t455\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210785\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Import legacy KV records instead of silently skipping them** When a legacy database contains the `kv` store, `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"kv\")` returns undefined because `legacyResourceMap` has no KV mapping, so this branch silently discards records such as `kv:globalPreferences`, `kv:preferences`, `kv:uiState`, and `kv:appMenu`. The recovery flow nevertheless persists an `import_old_data` decision and reports success, leaving migrated users with reset preferences and navigation state. Convert these records\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t461\t2026-08-30T23:51:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890895071\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Normalize renamed resource IDs during legacy import** For imports from renamed stores such as `goal`, `PointGoal`, `todo`, `PointTask`, or `combination`, the target table is changed to `objective`, `task`, or `space`, but the record ID is retained verbatim here; the added tests even preserve `goal:*` IDs in objective rows. DataFn's `determineResourceType()` returns the ID prefix literally, so selecting a recovered goal for `relateDatafnRecords()` yields resource `goal`, fails the supported-resource check, a\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t623\t2026-08-30T22:59:12Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890782300\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add a fallback when database enumeration is unavailable** On browsers or embedded WebViews that implement IndexedDB but not `indexedDB.databases()`, this returns `undefined`, causing `detectLegacyLocalData()` to report `isSupported: false`; `UserBaseLayer` then skips the recovery gate and starts with an empty DataFn database even though the active user's legacy `${userId}-1` or `${dapId}-1` database is still present. Probe the deterministic legacy database names when enumeration is unavailable so existing l\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1044\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210782\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Rehydrate binary values during legacy import** For legacy `file` records containing `Uint8Array`, `ArrayBuffer`, Blob, or File data, export replaces the bytes with a `__legacyIndexedDbType`/`dataBase64` marker, but this fallback imports that marker as a plain object instead of decoding it. The unchanged file consumers expect `Uint8Array` data, so recovered offline attachments and thumbnails become empty or unreadable even though the recovery UI reports success. Decode these marker types before constructing \nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1233\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t91a40ab57f\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075834\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve PointLog rows that predate session IDs** For legacy Pointron `PointLog` rows created before sessions were attached, `sessionId` is absent—the retained legacy `FocusLog` type still declares it optional—so this conversion silently drops otherwise valid `start`, `totalFocus`, and `totalBreak` history. Recovery then records a successful decision and suppresses future prompts because these pre-import omissions are not reported as skipped rows. The fresh evidence after the prior conversion is this explic\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1241\t2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\tpullfrog\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146946\tSessionless `PointLog` rows now receive a `sessionId`, but the import payload never creates the corresponding `session`. The remote schema enforces this required foreign key, and legacy streak rows concretely omit `sessionId`, so their recovery can fail instead of preserving them. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve sessionless PointLog rows without orphaned references ## Affected sites - `client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts:1233-1235` — invents a session foreign key without adding that session resource. - `shared/data/datafn/schema.datafn.ts:646-652` \nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1248\t2026-08-31T01:56:04Z\tpullfrog\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891224029\tThe exact sessionless rows cited by the original finding are created with `goalId: \"PointGoal:Empty\"`, but no matching goal exists. This converts that sentinel to `objective:Empty`, and the generated remote schema enforces `sessionLog.objectiveId` as a foreign key, so creating the synthetic session only moves the import failure to this relation. Drop the sentinel objective reference or create a matching supported resource, and add the exact streak-row fixture to verify the complete payload.\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t420\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201425\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clear DataFn data before destroying the runtime** When AuthFn account deletion succeeds, `signOut()` first calls `destroyNucleumDatafn()`, which clears `runtimeStore`; the following `clearDatafnLocalData()` immediately returns because there is no `runtime?.storage`. Consequently, deleting an account leaves its IndexedDB cache and user data on the device. Clear the active storage before signing out, or retain the storage handle through deletion. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21n\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213268\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject failed DataFn file metadata mutations** When an S3 upload succeeds but the following DataFn mutation resolves with `{ ok: false }`, this code ignores the result and returns `[file]` as though persistence succeeded. Callers such as `MediaGrid.uploadToS3()` then retain the returned file reference even though no file record exists, producing broken attachments; inspect the mutation result and propagate its error before returning success. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t883\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206083\t<!-- cubic:v=c6f81909-7a2d-4fa6-8b8c-2aab3b248bb0 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P2: `checkIfSessionExpired` removed the offline short-circuit that previously returned `false` whenever an offline session existed without an AuthFn token. A LOCAL/offline-only user (no AuthFn session) now goes through `resolveAuthSession()`, which can report the missing session as expired and kick them back to sign-in. Preserve the offline-only early return before calling `resolveAuthSession`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> \nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t903\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206105\t<!-- cubic:v=d6780195-cd6c-435a-9053-45a40c0c2247 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: When `isReturnUrl` is true, `saveLocalFile` still converts the entire blob into a Uint8Array (and decodes the thumbnail) before returning a `URL.createObjectURL`. For large files this copies the whole payload into memory for a result that only needs the blob URL, and the created object URL is never revoked, leaking it. Move the `isReturnUrl` early return before the arrayBuffer work, and revoke the object URL once consumed. <details> <summar\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t946\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213274\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unavailable sessions in extension checks** When AuthFn returns `unavailable` and the stored session is not eligible for cached-cloud use—for example, an extension has a bearer token but no cached `USER_INFO`, or offlinability is disabled—this returns `false`. `SheetBaseLayer.performSessionExpiryCheck()` and `ExtensionBaseLayer.checkIfSessionExpired()` interpret that as an active session and proceed to initialize authenticated extension data instead of showing the login/service error, so only authenti\nclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t603\t2026-08-31T00:20:17Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tbd15cad28d\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963087\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the create-space modal under the callers' action key** In the Nucleum and Memotron Spaces flows, the product configuration and library components still expose `Resource.combination`, so `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` dispatches `combination-create`; registering this modal only as `space-create` makes `appStore.resolveAction()` return null and the New space action does nothing. Keep a compatibility registration or migrate every caller, including `CreateCombination`'s `ModalFooter`, to the new key. AG\nclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t606\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t8739a79ce4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265058\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the space modal under the generated key** The fresh evidence in this revision is that the registration is now `combination-create`, while both shared `resourceAction()` implementations and callers such as `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` and `CreateCombination` generate `combination_create` with an underscore. Because the Memotron and Nucleum configurations still expose the legacy `Resource.combination`, selecting New space cannot resolve this modal and `runAction()` navigates to 404; register the gen\nclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t670\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321872\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map goal collection searches to objective** When “Add item to collection” is used for a Pointron goal collection or a goal-typed Nucleum collection, `Collection.svelte` passes the legacy `goal` resource here, but the DataFn schema exposes that resource as `objective`. Forwarding `goal` to `datafn.search()` makes non-empty searches fail or return no goals, even though the blank-query recents path has a compatibility mapping; translate `goal` to `objective` before searching. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6\nclient/stores/app.store.ts\t207\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321878\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the legacy goal route in the mobile menu gate** On portrait layouts, breadcrumb navigation still calls `gotoResource()` with legacy resource IDs and therefore produces paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers are migrated. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/n\nclient/stores/app.store.ts\t700\t2026-08-30T18:51:26Z\tcoderabbitai\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890231197\t_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_ **Remove dead commented-out code in the modified files.** Delete the inactive statement, declaration, and render block in `app.store.ts`, `userPreferences.store.ts`, and `UserLayout.svelte`. Keep any future behavior changes in a tracked follow-up rather than leaving disabled production code beside the active implementation. <details> <summary>📍 Affects 3 files</summary> - `client/stores/app.store.ts#L700-L700` (this comment) - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts#L14-L14` - `client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte#\nclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t64\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269356\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bulk relation mutations atomic** When one source in a bulk link operation fails or returns `{ ok: false }`, the other `Promise.all` mutations may already have committed before `assertMutationSucceeded` throws. The UI then reports the whole operation as failed even though some records were linked, and retrying can encounter duplicates; use a transactional batch mutation or compensate the successful mutations before propagating the failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\nclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t137\t2026-08-30T23:23:45Z\tpullfrog\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890834875\t`datafn.transact` bypasses DataFn's local/offline mutation path and always invokes the remote adapter. Local-only accounts and offline cloud sessions configure no remote adapter, so add-to-collection and bulk-link actions now throw instead of updating local storage. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve relation actions without a 