{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:54:00.385Z","ordinal":8580,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_07a651664efba6ab016a94ecc5580887d0a7bdf79df7d19780","status":"completed","call_id":"call_U4c7SVqQVCfSjC3axPsLOoF3","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-64885893.dTR4ys\\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \\\"\\\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \\\"\\\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \\\"\\\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \\\"\\\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[0:12][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\\\"[\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+\\\";\\\" \\\")|.[0:700])] | @tsv' \\\"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\\\"\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-570-review\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 12000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a055b1-b0ee-7061-8828-4da29bf187dc","create_time":1788144835.019002}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:54:00.474Z","ordinal":8581,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a053e7-239f-7703-8a5b-d9d8ac22d6de","turn_id":"01a055b1-b0ee-7061-8828-4da29bf187dc","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ad87f28b-a98b-46c0-a5d2-8b72fdb386e0","process_id":"91832","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-64885893.dTR4ys\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \"\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \"\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \"\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \"\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[0:12][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\"[\\\\r\\\\n]+\";\" \")|.[0:700])] | @tsv' \"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\""],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-570-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-64885893.dTR4ys\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \"\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \"\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \"\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \"\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[0:12][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\"[\\\\r\\\\n]+\";\" \")|.[0:700])] | @tsv' \"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"0\tclient/components/account/auth.ts\t238\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions** For users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to enter an empty guest namespace instead of remaining signed out. Remove the stale offline marker as part of expiration, while preserving it only for accounts explicitly created in o\n1\tclient/components/record/recent.store.ts\t128\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table** For Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \"search\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compatibility mapping already used elsewhere. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/0383892256c226cd46b9f6b840ab704b0a4900a2/AGENTS.md#L6-L7) Usef\n2\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t66\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122431\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode** When a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude `sync-direct` here or make the flow enable offlinability before setup. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n3\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t120\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827057\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid clone-up for local-only restores** When an offline-only account or a cloud account currently in offline mode restores a backup, this always requests `triggerCloneUp` even though the active runtime has no remote transport. The import can therefore fail after writing local rows, leaving the UI reporting failure with a partially restored database; the legacy recovery path already avoids this by enabling clone-up only when `runtime.mode === \"sync\"`. Apply the same mode check here. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2d59ba577bb954a82d823d6125aa1e0b79a2c38c/AGEN\n4\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t28\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122432\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Recompute network state after reconnecting** If Sync Settings is mounted while the browser is offline and then the connection returns, `isNetworkInducedOfflineMode` remains the mount-time value `true`. Although `BaseLayer` updates `$context.isInOfflineMode` to false, this new toggle therefore stays disabled until the settings component is remounted, preventing the user from changing offline availability after reconnecting. Derive this value from reactive connectivity state rather than the fixed `navigator.onLine` snapshot. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n5\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t79\t2026-08-30T22:59:12Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890782302\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Delete the local clone when disabling offlinability** When a sync user turns off “Keep data available offline,” this initialization only closes the current adapter and switches to `sync-direct`; neither this handler nor the runtime teardown deletes or clears the retired IndexedDB database. The device therefore retains the user's complete local clone indefinitely despite the setting promising that no local copy is kept; after pending changes are flushed, delete the old namespace database as part of the transition. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/d6d85ebdb1daf5\n6\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t86\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206029\t<!-- cubic:v=87316749-6b84-4f09-9f38-a848d86455fd --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P2: When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offline storage, but this switch still accepts and persists `false`. Disable the switch while E2EE is enabled, or reject the change without persisting it. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte, line 69: <comment>When E2EE is enabled, DataFn always requires offline storage, but this switch still accepts and persists `false`. Disable the switch whi\n7\tclient/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\t186\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206015\t<!-- cubic:v=192b913b-f3f8-4c32-bbaa-410bc61d68cf --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} --> P1: Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts, line 181: <comment>Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqu\n8\tclient/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\t298\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269353\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply the historical timezone correction instead of a round trip** When a Pointron user has timezone-change records, `AnalyticsCardView` and `AnalyticsChartStandalone` depend on this method to normalize historical session timestamps. Resolving date parts in a timezone and immediately resolving those same parts back in the same timezone returns the original instant, so the correction is effectively a no-op and sessions can be grouped or filtered into the wrong day after travel; the conversion needs to account for the historical-to-current timezone difference. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n9\tclient/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts\t129\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265052\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore writable updates for preference bindings** Svelte compiles assignments and bindings such as those in `SizeFactorSetting`, `AppearanceSettings`, `DateTimeSettings`, and `CmdResults` into calls to `userPreferences.set(...)`, but this replacement exposes only `subscribe`, `get`, and `modify`. When users change sizing, popup blur, time scales, day-start values, or recent commands, the generated handler therefore fails instead of updating and persisting the preference; restore a persistence-aware `set` method or migrate every direct `$userPreferences` assignment. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13\n10\tclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t48\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827049\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore the Nucleum entitlement gate after authentication** For cloud users opening the Nucleum product, this replacement admits every successful session without the prior `account.ping()` and `PlanType.NUCLEUS` check. A repo-wide search finds no remaining navigation to `/error/access-denied`, and AuthFn session resolution does not populate or enforce the account plan, so users with only a Memotron or Pointron entitlement can enter the combined Nucleum UI. Restore the product-specific entitlement check after authentication. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2d59b\n11\tclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t92\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075826\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow cached Nucleum sessions to use their offline clone** When a Nucleum cloud user with offlinability enabled launches during a network outage or manual offline mode, `resolveAuthSession()` deliberately returns `cached-cloud`, but this branch unconditionally sends them to access denied without consulting any cached entitlement. Unlike the prior gate, which only denied a known non-Nucleum plan, this locks every entitled Nucleum user out of the local clone whenever the account service cannot be reached. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/91a40ab57f575d1eed347dcb7a\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"0\tclient/components/account/auth.ts\t238\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions** For users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to enter an empty guest namespace instead of remaining signed out. Remove the stale offline marker as part of expiration, while preserving it only for accounts explicitly created in o\n1\tclient/components/record/recent.store.ts\t128\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table** For Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \"search\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compatibility mapping already used elsewhere. AGENTS.md reference: [A