r total resource counts and node subtypes. The previous `CollectionCache` action was removed, and repo-wide search shows it is now mounted only by the clipper, leaving no host-app producer for `collection-item-counts` or `typed-collection-cache`; consequently collection item badges and typed-collection avatars remain empty. Retain the shared collection cache until equivalent DataFn relation signals populate those keys. AGENTS.md refe\n21\tclient/layout/layers/cache/cache.store.ts\t18\t2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891015247\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep dispatching cache update events** When DataFn resource-count or node-subtype signals emit after a consumer has mounted, `cache.replace()` now updates only the internal store. Consumers such as `ResourceSwitcherItem` and `LibrarySubTypeSwitcher` read via `cache.retrieve()` rather than subscribing to the store, and rely exclusively on `ComponentBaseLayer`'s `cacheUpdate` event to refresh, so their displayed counts remain at the initial value after creates, deletes, archives, or syncs. Preserve the event contract or migrate these consumers to subscribe directly. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n22\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t164\t2026-08-31T00:20:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963089\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Convert legacy timezone rows during recovery** For migrated Pointron or Nucleum users with records in the legacy `tz` store, this map has no timezone target, so `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"tz\")` returns undefined and recovery silently skips the history even though detection recognizes `tz` as a legacy resource store. The replacement timezone store reads only `datafn.temporal.listTimezoneChanges()`, leaving historical timezone corrections unavailable and causing analytics around earlier timezone changes to be grouped incorrectly after upgrade. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21\n23\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t173\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827046\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Translate PointLog fields before importing** For old Pointron databases containing `PointLog`, mapping the store directly to `sessionLog` is insufficient: historical rows use fields such as `totalFocus`, `totalBreak`, `start`, and `goalId`, while the DataFn schema requires modern fields including `startUnix`, `endUnix`, and `sessionId`. The current transform only renames `goalId`, so filtering against the schema drops the focus metrics and the required-field failures cause these rows to be skipped, preventing recovery of historical analytics. Add a dedicated `PointLog` conversion before importing. AGENTS.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2708},"formatted_output":"12\tclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t178\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122427\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the cached plan when entitlement refresh fails** When an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the plan endpoint is temporarily unavailable, the account update immediately above has already cleared the cached plan and this condition treats the missing response as a failed entitlement. Entitled Nucleum users are consequently redirected to access denied despite the newly persisted `USER_PLAN`; fall back to that validated cached plan on refresh failures while continuing to deny a known non-Nucleum plan. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.\n13\tclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t461\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269351\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve manual offline mode across connectivity events** When a user has explicitly enabled offline mode and the browser reconnects, this handler derives `isOffline` solely from `navigator.onLine`, overwrites the stored-mode state, and switches DataFn back to sync. The reconnect can therefore upload locally queued changes despite the user's offline-mode selection; combine network state with `ClientStorageKey.OFFLINE_MODE` before updating the runtime, and invoke the same runtime update when the manual toggle changes. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/589009fcb9\n14\tclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t609\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206027\t<!-- cubic:v=74adb245-1155-4663-8f26-acad72481976 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P2: Removing this `<span id=\"global-sync-status\">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById(\"global-sync-status\")?.getAttribute(\"data-syncstatus\")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync listener no longer reflects the current global sync status on initial load. Update `SyncStatusListener.r\n15\tclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t176\t2026-08-30T23:51:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t9aadca2ea9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890895070\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bridge legacy Flux mutations into DataFn** When unchanged flows such as `nodeStore.create()` or `taskStore.create()` run, `ResourceStore` writes to the Dexie-backed legacy `flux`, not `datafn`. This call starts that independent runtime after DataFn, but nothing imports subsequent Flux mutations; additionally, `SyncLayer.svelte` now invokes only `pullDatafnNow()`, and repo-wide search finds no remaining `flux.sync()` call. Thus newly created or edited records can remain outside DataFn search/cache and never reach the DataFn remote. The fresh evidence in this revision is that Flux is initialized again witho\n16\tclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t329\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213265\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Confirm native backup delivery before suppressing recovery** In an embedded iOS/macOS recovery flow, `downloadLegacyLocalBackup()` starts the asynchronous `fileStore.downloadFromBlob()` upload/handoff without awaiting or validating it, and this branch immediately saves `download_backup_continue`. If the upload fails or returns no URL, the UI still reports success and permanently suppresses the startup recovery prompt even though the user received no backup; make the helper report delivery success and await it before saving the decision. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nuc\n17\tclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t439\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213269\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore automatic timezone-change capture** When a Pointron or Nucleum user travels and later focuses the app, `onAppear()` no longer detects or records the browser timezone change; the former `refreshTimeZone()` call was removed, and repo-wide search finds no remaining automatic caller of `userPreferences.setTimeZone()`. Consequently DataFn's temporal history remains stale, so calendar boundaries and historical analytics continue using the previous zone unless the user manually changes settings. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd\n18\tclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t576\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201424\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep Flux initialized until all product stores migrate** In the normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron app flow, this now initializes only DataFn, while numerous unchanged product stores still call the exported legacy `flux` instance—for example, `ResourceStore.create()` invokes `flux.mutation()` and node/history code invokes `flux.selectMany()`. That export remains a null cast until `initFlux()` runs, and repo-wide search shows initialization now occurs only in sheet and extension flows, so ordinary create, edit, and select interactions fail at runtime even though DataFn startup succeeds. Keep the compat\n19\tclient/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte\t30\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206079\t<!-- cubic:v=3305c83a-6926-4b7c-a3d0-8b2dda285386 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P2: This import makes `AccessMode.POP` passed to `ResourceResolver` a different enum type from its `accessMode` prop, causing the app type check to fail. Keep the legacy import until `ResourceResolver` migrates too, or migrate both together. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte, line 30: <comment>This import makes `AccessMode.POP` passed to `ResourceResolver` a different enum type from its `accessMode` pro\n20\tclient/layout/layers/cache/InMemoryCache.svelte\t37\t2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891015251\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the collection cache mounted in host apps** In normal Nucleum, Memotron, and Pointron flows, this replacement mounts only the global calendar cache and creates signals for total resource counts and node subtypes. The previous `CollectionCache` action was removed, and repo-wide search shows it is now mounted only by the clipper, leaving no host-app producer for `collection-item-counts` or `typed-collection-cache`; consequently collection item badges and typed-collection avatars remain empty. Retain the shared collection cache until equivalent DataFn relation signals populate those keys. AGENTS.md refe\n21\tclient/layout/layers/cache/cache.store.ts\t18\t2026-08-31T00:39:54Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891015247\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep dispatching cache update events** When DataFn resource-count or node-subtype signals emit after a consumer has mounted, `cache.replace()` now updates only the internal store. Consumers such as `ResourceSwitcherItem` and `LibrarySubTypeSwitcher` read via `cache.retrieve()` rather than subscribing to the store, and rely exclusively on `ComponentBaseLayer`'s `cacheUpdate` event to refresh, so their displayed counts remain at the initial value after creates, deletes, archives, or syncs. Preserve the event contract or migrate these consumers to subscribe directly. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n22\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t164\t2026-08-31T00:20:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963089\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Convert legacy timezone rows during recovery** For migrated Pointron or Nucleum users with records in the legacy `tz` store, this map has no timezone target, so `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"tz\")` returns undefined and recovery silently skips the history even though detection recognizes `tz` as a legacy resource store. The replacement timezone store reads only `datafn.temporal.listTimezoneChanges()`, leaving historical timezone corrections unavailable and causing analytics around earlier timezone changes to be grouped incorrectly after upgrade. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21\n23\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t173\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827046\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Translate PointLog fields before importing** For old Pointron databases containing `PointLog`, mapping the store directly to `sessionLog` is insufficient: historical rows use fields such as `totalFocus`, `totalBreak`, `start`, and `goalId`, while the DataFn schema requires modern fields including `startUnix`, `endUnix`, and `sessionId`. The current transform only renames `goalId`, so filtering against the schema drops the focus metrics and the required-field failures cause these rows to be skipped, preventing recovery of historical analytics. Add a dedicated `PointLog` conversion before importing. AGENTS.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788144846448,"completed_at_ms":1788144846448}}
