em. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve sessionless PointLog rows without orphaned references ## Affected sites - `client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts:1233-1235` — invents a session foreign key without adding that session resource. - `shared/data/datafn/schema.datafn.ts:646-652` — declares `sessionLog.sessionId` as the required relation to `session`. - `services/account/src/db/\n31\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1248\t2026-08-31T01:56:04Z\tpullfrog\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891224029\tThe exact sessionless rows cited by the original finding are created with `goalId: \"PointGoal:Empty\"`, but no matching goal exists. This converts that sentinel to `objective:Empty`, and the generated remote schema enforces `sessionLog.objectiveId` as a foreign key, so creating the synthetic session only moves the import failure to this relation. Drop the sentinel objective reference or create a matching supported resource, and add the exact streak-row fixture to verify the complete payload.\n32\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t420\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201425\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clear DataFn data before destroying the runtime** When AuthFn account deletion succeeds, `signOut()` first calls `destroyNucleumDatafn()`, which clears `runtimeStore`; the following `clearDatafnLocalData()` immediately returns because there is no `runtime?.storage`. Consequently, deleting an account leaves its IndexedDB cache and user data on the device. Clear the active storage before signing out, or retain the storage handle through deletion. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L12-L13) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎\n33\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213268\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject failed DataFn file metadata mutations** When an S3 upload succeeds but the following DataFn mutation resolves with `{ ok: false }`, this code ignores the result and returns `[file]` as though persistence succeeded. Callers such as `MediaGrid.uploadToS3()` then retain the returned file reference even though no file record exists, producing broken attachments; inspect the mutation result and propagate its error before returning success. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/AGENTS.md#L12-L13) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n34\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t883\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206083\t<!-- cubic:v=c6f81909-7a2d-4fa6-8b8c-2aab3b248bb0 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P2: `checkIfSessionExpired` removed the offline short-circuit that previously returned `false` whenever an offline session existed without an AuthFn token. A LOCAL/offline-only user (no AuthFn session) now goes through `resolveAuthSession()`, which can report the missing session as expired and kick them back to sign-in. Preserve the offline-only early return before calling `resolveAuthSession`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/stores\n35\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t903\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206105\t<!-- cubic:v=d6780195-cd6c-435a-9053-45a40c0c2247 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: When `isReturnUrl` is true, `saveLocalFile` still converts the entire blob into a Uint8Array (and decodes the thumbnail) before returning a `URL.createObjectURL`. For large files this copies the whole payload into memory for a result that only needs the blob URL, and the created object URL is never revoked, leaking it. Move the `isReturnUrl` early return before the arrayBuffer work, and revoke the object URL once consumed. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root c\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2792},"formatted_output":"24\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t396\t2026-08-29T10:00:24Z\tpullfrog\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886218145\tLegacy Dexie databases are named `${userOrDapId}-1`, but this accepts every `*-1` database while [`detectLegacyLocalData()`](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts#L201-L235) enumerates the whole browser. On a shared device, account B can therefore import account A's records into B's DataFn namespace; discovery and import need to be scoped to the active identity. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Scope legacy recovery to the signed-in identity ## Affected sites - `client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts:201-235` scans every IndexedDB descriptor. - `client/persistence/legacyLocal\n25\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t455\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210785\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Import legacy KV records instead of silently skipping them** When a legacy database contains the `kv` store, `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"kv\")` returns undefined because `legacyResourceMap` has no KV mapping, so this branch silently discards records such as `kv:globalPreferences`, `kv:preferences`, `kv:uiState`, and `kv:appMenu`. The recovery flow nevertheless persists an `import_old_data` decision and reports success, leaving migrated users with reset preferences and navigation state. Convert these records through the DataFn KV representation before completing recovery. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L1\n26\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t461\t2026-08-30T23:51:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890895071\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Normalize renamed resource IDs during legacy import** For imports from renamed stores such as `goal`, `PointGoal`, `todo`, `PointTask`, or `combination`, the target table is changed to `objective`, `task`, or `space`, but the record ID is retained verbatim here; the added tests even preserve `goal:*` IDs in objective rows. DataFn's `determineResourceType()` returns the ID prefix literally, so selecting a recovered goal for `relateDatafnRecords()` yields resource `goal`, fails the supported-resource check, and similar prefix-dispatched operations target the wrong table. Rewrite record IDs and every corresp\n27\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t623\t2026-08-30T22:59:12Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890782300\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add a fallback when database enumeration is unavailable** On browsers or embedded WebViews that implement IndexedDB but not `indexedDB.databases()`, this returns `undefined`, causing `detectLegacyLocalData()` to report `isSupported: false`; `UserBaseLayer` then skips the recovery gate and starts with an empty DataFn database even though the active user's legacy `${userId}-1` or `${dapId}-1` database is still present. Probe the deterministic legacy database names when enumeration is unavailable so existing local-only users do not lose access to their data after upgrading. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L1\n28\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1044\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210782\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Rehydrate binary values during legacy import** For legacy `file` records containing `Uint8Array`, `ArrayBuffer`, Blob, or File data, export replaces the bytes with a `__legacyIndexedDbType`/`dataBase64` marker, but this fallback imports that marker as a plain object instead of decoding it. The unchanged file consumers expect `Uint8Array` data, so recovered offline attachments and thumbnails become empty or unreadable even though the recovery UI reports success. Decode these marker types before constructing the DataFn import payload. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum\n29\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1233\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t91a40ab57f\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075834\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve PointLog rows that predate session IDs** For legacy Pointron `PointLog` rows created before sessions were attached, `sessionId` is absent—the retained legacy `FocusLog` type still declares it optional—so this conversion silently drops otherwise valid `start`, `totalFocus`, and `totalBreak` history. Recovery then records a successful decision and suppresses future prompts because these pre-import omissions are not reported as skipped rows. The fresh evidence after the prior conversion is this explicit rejection of every row lacking `sessionId`; generate a deterministic legacy session reference or \n30\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1241\t2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\tpullfrog\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146946\tSessionless `PointLog` rows now receive a `sessionId`, but the import payload never creates the corresponding `session`. The remote schema enforces this required foreign key, and legacy streak rows concretely omit `sessionId`, so their recovery can fail instead of preserving them. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve sessionless PointLog rows without orphaned references ## Affected sites - `client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts:1233-1235` — invents a session foreign key without adding that session resource. - `shared/data/datafn/schema.datafn.ts:646-652` — declares `sessionLog.sessionId` as the required relation to `session`. - `services/account/src/db/\n31\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1248\t2026-08-31T01:56:04Z\tpullfrog\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891224029\tThe exact sessionless rows cited by the original finding are created with `goalId: \"PointGoal:Empty\"`, but no matching goal exists. This converts that sentinel to `objective:Empty`, and the generated remote schema enforces `sessionLog.objectiveId` as a foreign key, so creating the synthetic session only moves the import failure to this relation. Drop the sentinel objective reference or create a matching supported resource, and add the exact streak-row fixture to verify the complete payload.\n32\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t420\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201425\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clear DataFn data before destroying the runtime** When AuthFn account deletion succeeds, `signOut()` first calls `destroyNucleumDatafn()`, which clears `runtimeStore`; the following `clearDatafnLocalData()` immediately returns because there is no `runtime?.storage`. Consequently, deleting an account leaves its IndexedDB cache and user data on the device. Clear the active storage before signing out, or retain the storage handle through deletion. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/e28a5819c6abd13f1ce97f4ab2e8a277ff22b9d1/AGENTS.md#L12-L13) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎\n33\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213268\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject failed DataFn file metadata mutations** When an S3 upload succeeds but the following DataFn mutation resolves with `{ ok: false }`, this code ignores the result and returns `[file]` as though persistence succeeded. Callers such as `MediaGrid.uploadToS3()` then retain the returned file reference even though no file record exists, producing broken attachments; inspect the mutation result and propagate its error before returning success. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/ce677ed4a45f3dd9a2f5c9137cd0da7fd5ca403b/AGENTS.md#L12-L13) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n34\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t883\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206083\t<!-- cubic:v=c6f81909-7a2d-4fa6-8b8c-2aab3b248bb0 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P2: `checkIfSessionExpired` removed the offline short-circuit that previously returned `false` whenever an offline session existed without an AuthFn token. A LOCAL/offline-only user (no AuthFn session) now goes through `resolveAuthSession()`, which can report the missing session as expired and kick them back to sign-in. Preserve the offline-only early return before calling `resolveAuthSession`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agent