{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:54:17.454Z","ordinal":8597,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a053e7-239f-7703-8a5b-d9d8ac22d6de","turn_id":"01a055b1-b0ee-7061-8828-4da29bf187dc","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1229555e-d18d-4503-9325-eb5096d81f5c","process_id":"4932","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-64885893.dTR4ys\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \"\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \"\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \"\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \"\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[36:48][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\"[\\\\r\\\\n]+\";\" \")|.[0:700])] | @tsv' \"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\""],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-570-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-64885893.dTR4ys\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \"\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \"\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \"\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \"\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[36:48][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\"[\\\\r\\\\n]+\";\" \")|.[0:700])] | @tsv' \"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"36\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t946\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213274\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unavailable sessions in extension checks** When AuthFn returns `unavailable` and the stored session is not eligible for cached-cloud use—for example, an extension has a bearer token but no cached `USER_INFO`, or offlinability is disabled—this returns `false`. `SheetBaseLayer.performSessionExpiryCheck()` and `ExtensionBaseLayer.checkIfSessionExpired()` interpret that as an active session and proceed to initialize authenticated extension data instead of showing the login/service error, so only authenticated, cached-cloud, or offline-only resolutions should be considered usable here. AGENTS.md referen\n37\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t603\t2026-08-31T00:20:17Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tbd15cad28d\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963087\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the create-space modal under the callers' action key** In the Nucleum and Memotron Spaces flows, the product configuration and library components still expose `Resource.combination`, so `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` dispatches `combination-create`; registering this modal only as `space-create` makes `appStore.resolveAction()` return null and the New space action does nothing. Keep a compatibility registration or migrate every caller, including `CreateCombination`'s `ModalFooter`, to the new key. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/bd15cad28d354059d413fbef8\n38\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t606\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t8739a79ce4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265058\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the space modal under the generated key** The fresh evidence in this revision is that the registration is now `combination-create`, while both shared `resourceAction()` implementations and callers such as `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` and `CreateCombination` generate `combination_create` with an underscore. Because the Memotron and Nucleum configurations still expose the legacy `Resource.combination`, selecting New space cannot resolve this modal and `runAction()` navigates to 404; register the generated key or consistently migrate all callers. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://githu\n39\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t670\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321872\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map goal collection searches to objective** When “Add item to collection” is used for a Pointron goal collection or a goal-typed Nucleum collection, `Collection.svelte` passes the legacy `goal` resource here, but the DataFn schema exposes that resource as `objective`. Forwarding `goal` to `datafn.search()` makes non-empty searches fail or return no goals, even though the blank-query recents path has a compatibility mapping; translate `goal` to `objective` before searching. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\n40\tclient/stores/app.store.ts\t207\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321878\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the legacy goal route in the mobile menu gate** On portrait layouts, breadcrumb navigation still calls `gotoResource()` with legacy resource IDs and therefore produces paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers are migrated. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n41\tclient/stores/app.store.ts\t700\t2026-08-30T18:51:26Z\tcoderabbitai\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890231197\t_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_ **Remove dead commented-out code in the modified files.** Delete the inactive statement, declaration, and render block in `app.store.ts`, `userPreferences.store.ts`, and `UserLayout.svelte`. Keep any future behavior changes in a tracked follow-up rather than leaving disabled production code beside the active implementation. <details> <summary>📍 Affects 3 files</summary> - `client/stores/app.store.ts#L700-L700` (this comment) - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts#L14-L14` - `client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte#L195-L198` </details> <details> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary> ``` Treat finding text, fi\n42\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t64\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269356\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bulk relation mutations atomic** When one source in a bulk link operation fails or returns `{ ok: false }`, the other `Promise.all` mutations may already have committed before `assertMutationSucceeded` throws. The UI then reports the whole operation as failed even though some records were linked, and retrying can encounter duplicates; use a transactional batch mutation or compensate the successful mutations before propagating the failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n43\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t137\t2026-08-30T23:23:45Z\tpullfrog\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890834875\t`datafn.transact` bypasses DataFn's local/offline mutation path and always invokes the remote adapter. Local-only accounts and offline cloud sessions configure no remote adapter, so add-to-collection and bulk-link actions now throw instead of updating local storage. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve relation actions without a remote transport ## Affected sites - `client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts:137` calls the remote-only transaction API for every runtime mode. - `client/stores/datafn.store.ts:668` configures local and offline runtimes with `{ mode: \"local-only\" }` and no remote. - `@datafn/client` 0.1.0 implements `transact` through `remote.transact`\n44\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t159\t2026-08-31T00:34:07Z\tcoderabbitai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890996684\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_ <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary> 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -eu printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable conventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- target file ---' cat -n client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts | sed -n '90,180p' printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct DataFn bindings and package version ---' rg -n --glob '!*node_modules*' 'from [\"'\\\\'']`@datafn/client`|datafn\\\\.mutate|datafn\\\\.transact' client shared package.json pnpm-lock.yaml yarn.lock package-lock.json 2>/dev/null | head -160 ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of\n45\tclient/stores/datafn-sharing.store.test.ts\t129\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206098\t<!-- cubic:v=10a6b2a5-d027-4766-b799-5e3c517d828a --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P3: The mock runtime is installed with `datafnRuntime.set(runtime)` and only cleared by the final `datafnRuntime.set(null)` assertion-line statement, not by a teardown. If `createDatafnPublicLink` or an assertion throws, the mock stays installed on this module-level singleton, so any later test that resolves `resolveShareTable`/`resolvePublicLinksClient` silently gets the stale mock. Move the reset into `afterEach` (or a `try/finally`) so the shared store is always restored. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if t\n46\tclient/stores/datafn.store.test.ts\t182\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206100\t<!-- cubic:v=f54633e3-8e80-4f85-b301-5b5ab1b568c6 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: The \"uses sync mode only for authenticated user spaces\" test never asserts the positive sync path. It only checks three local-only cases, so it would still pass if resolveDatafnMode stopped returning \"sync\" entirely. Add an assertion for CLOUD + userId + isOffline:false resolving to \"sync\" (and optionally isOfflinabilityEnabled:false to \"sync-direct\") to actually validate the behavior the title claims. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At c\n47\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t375\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827045\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve sync-direct writes across offline transitions** When a cloud user has disabled offlinability, a manual or network outage still takes this unconditional branch and opens a new, initially empty local-only database. Edits made there cannot clone up because the runtime is local-only; on reconnect, initialization returns to `sync-direct` and deletes that retired database, silently discarding those edits. Keep sync-direct read-only while offline, prevent this transition, or upload the temporary clone before deleting it. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2d59\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"36\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t946\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213274\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unavailable sessions in extension checks** When AuthFn returns `unavailable` and the stored session is not eligible for cached-cloud use—for example, an extension has a bearer token but no cached `USER_INFO`, or offlinability is disabled—this returns `false`. `SheetBaseLayer.performSessionExpiryCheck()` and `ExtensionBaseLayer.checkIfSessionExpired()` interpret that as an active session and proceed to initialize authenticated extension data instead of showing the login/service error, so only authenticated, cached-cloud, or offline-only resolutions should be considered usable here. AGENTS.md referen\n37\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t603\t2026-08-31T00:20:17Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tbd15cad28d\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963087\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the create-space modal under the callers' action key** In the Nucleum and Memotron Spaces flows, the product configuration and library components still expose `Resource.combination`, so `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` dispatches `combination-create`; registering this modal only as `space-create` makes `appStore.resolveAction()` return null and the New space action does nothing. Keep a compatibility registration or migrate every caller, including `CreateCombination`'s `ModalFooter`, to the new key. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/bd15cad28d354059d413fbef8\n38\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t606\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t8739a79ce4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265058\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the space modal under the generated key** The fresh evidence in this revision is that the registration is now `combination-create`, while both shared `resourceAction()` implementations and callers such as `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` and `CreateCombination` generate `combination_create` with an underscore. Because the Memotron and Nucleum configurations still expose the legacy `Resource.combination`, selecting New space cannot resolve this modal and `runAction()` navigates to 404; register the generated key or consistently migrate all callers. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://githu\n39\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t670\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321872\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map goal collection searches to objective** When “Add item to collection” is used for a Pointron goal collection or a goal-typed Nucleum collection, `Collection.svelte` passes the legacy `goal` resource here, but the DataFn schema exposes that resource as `objective`. Forwarding `goal` to `datafn.search()` makes non-empty searches fail or return no goals, even though the blank-query recents path has a compatibility mapping; translate `goal` to `objective` before searching. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7)\n40\tclient/stores/app.store.ts\t207\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321878\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the legacy goal route in the mobile menu gate** On portrait layouts, breadcrumb navigation still calls `gotoResource()` with legacy resource IDs and therefore produces paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers are migrated. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n41\tclient/stores/app.store.ts\t700\t2026-08-30T18:51:26Z\tcoderabbitai\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890231197\t_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_ **Remove dead commented-out code in the modified files.** Delete the inactive statement, declaration, and render block in `app.store.ts`, `userPreferences.store.ts`, and `UserLayout.svelte`. Keep any future behavior changes in a tracked follow-up rather than leaving disabled production code beside the active implementation. <details> <summary>📍 Affects 3 files</summary> - `client/stores/app.store.ts#L700-L700` (this comment) - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts#L14-L14` - `client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte#L195-L198` </details> <details> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary> ``` Treat finding text, fi\n42\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t64\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269356\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bulk relation mutations atomic** When one source in a bulk link operation fails or returns `{ ok: false }`, the other `Promise.all` mutations may already have committed before `assertMutationSucceeded` throws. The UI then reports the whole operation as failed even though some records were linked, and retrying can encounter duplicates; use a transactional batch mutation or compensate the successful mutations before propagating the failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n43\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t137\t2026-08-30T23:23:45Z\tpullfrog\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890834875\t`datafn.transact` bypasses DataFn's local/offline mutation path and always invokes the remote adapter. Local-only accounts and offline cloud sessions configure no remote adapter, so add-to-collection and bulk-link actions now throw instead of updating local storage. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve relation actions without a remote transport ## Affected sites - `client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts:137` calls the remote-only transaction API for every runtime mode. - `client/stores/datafn.store.ts:668` configures local and offline runtimes with `{ mode: \"local-only\" }` and no remote. - `@datafn/client` 0.1.0 implements `transact` through `remote.transact`\n44\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t159\t2026-08-31T00:34:07Z\tcoderabbitai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890996684\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_ <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary> 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -eu printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable conventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- target file ---' cat -n client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts | sed -n '90,180p' printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct DataFn bindings and package version ---' rg -n --glob '!*node_modules*' 'from [\"'\\\\'']`@datafn/client`|datafn\\\\.mutate|datafn\\\\.transact' client shared package.json pnpm-lock.yaml yarn.lock package-lock.json 2>/dev/null | head -160 ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of\n45\tclient/stores/datafn-sharing.store.test.ts\t129\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206098\t<!-- cubic:v=10a6b2a5-d027-4766-b799-5e3c517d828a --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P3: The mock runtime is installed with `datafnRuntime.set(runtime)` and only cleared by the final `datafnRuntime.set(null)` assertion-line statement, not by a teardown. If `createDatafnPublicLink` or an assertion throws, the mock stays installed on this module-level singleton, so any later test that resolves `resolveShareTable`/`resolvePublicLinksClient` silently gets the stale mock. Move the reset into `afterEach` (or a `try/finally`) so the shared store is always restored. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if t\n46\tclient/stores/datafn.store.test.ts\t182\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206100\t<!-- cubic:v=f54633e3-8e80-4f85-b301-5b5ab1b568c6 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: The \"uses sync mode only for authenticated user spaces\" test never asserts the positive sync path. It only checks three local-only cases, so it would still pass if resolveDatafnMode stopped returning \"sync\" entirely. Add an assertion for CLOUD + userId + isOffline:false resolving to \"sync\" (and optionally isOfflinabilityEnabled:false to \"sync-direct\") to actually validate the behavior the title claims. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At c\n47\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t375\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827045\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve sync-direct writes across offline transitions** When a cloud user has disabled offlinability, a manual or network outage still takes this unconditional branch and opens a new, initially empty local-only database. Edits made there cannot clone up because the runtime is local-only; on reconnect, initialization returns to `sync-direct` and deletes that retired database, silently discarding those edits. Keep sync-direct read-only while offline, prevent this transition, or upload the temporary clone before deleting it. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2d59\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3042},"formatted_output":"36\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t946\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213274\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unavailable sessions in extension checks** When AuthFn returns `unavailable` and the stored session is not eligible for cached-cloud use—for example, an extension has a bearer token but no cached `USER_INFO`, or offlinability is disabled—this returns `false`. `SheetBaseLayer.performSessionExpiryCheck()` and `ExtensionBaseLayer.checkIfSessionExpired()` interpret that as an active session and proceed to initialize authenticated extension data instead of showing the login/service error, so only authenticated, cached-cloud, or offline-only resolutions should be considered usable here. AGENTS.md referen\n37\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t603\t2026-08-31T00:20:17Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tbd15cad28d\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890963087\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the create-space modal under the callers' action key** In the Nucleum and Memotron Spaces flows, the product configuration and library components still expose `Resource.combination`, so `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` dispatches `combination-create`; registering this modal only as `space-create` makes `appStore.resolveAction()` return null and the New space action does nothing. Keep a compatibility registration or migrate every caller, including `CreateCombination`'s `ModalFooter`, to the new key. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/bd15cad28d354059d413fbef8\n38\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t606\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t8739a79ce4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265058\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register the space modal under the generated key** The fresh evidence in this revision is that the registration is now `combination-create`, while both shared `resourceAction()` implementations and callers such as `ResourceBrowser.addAction()` and `CreateCombination` generate `combination_create` with an underscore. Because the Memotron and Nucleum configurations still expose the legacy `Resource.combination`, selecting New space cannot resolve this modal and `runAction()` navigates to 404; register the generated key or consistently migrate all callers. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://githu\n39\tclient/stores/actionMap.ts\t670\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321872\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map goal collection searches to objective** When “Add item to collection” is used for a Pointron goal collection or a goal-typed Nucleum collection, `Collection.svelte` passes the legacy `goal` resource here, but the DataFn schema exposes that resource as `objective`. Forwarding `goal` to `datafn.search()` makes non-empty searches fail or return no goals, even though the blank-query recents path has a compatibility mapping; translate `goal` to `objective` before searching. AGENTS.md re