P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the legacy goal route in the mobile menu gate** On portrait layouts, breadcrumb navigation still calls `gotoResource()` with legacy resource IDs and therefore produces paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers are migrated. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L6-L7](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/fa3b44579e8902366c0c170f9988949cb1c58311/AGENTS.md#L6-L7) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n41\tclient/stores/app.store.ts\t700\t2026-08-30T18:51:26Z\tcoderabbitai\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890231197\t_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_ **Remove dead commented-out code in the modified files.** Delete the inactive statement, declaration, and render block in `app.store.ts`, `userPreferences.store.ts`, and `UserLayout.svelte`. Keep any future behavior changes in a tracked follow-up rather than leaving disabled production code beside the active implementation. <details> <summary>📍 Affects 3 files</summary> - `client/stores/app.store.ts#L700-L700` (this comment) - `client/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts#L14-L14` - `client/layout/layers/UserLayout.svelte#L195-L198` </details> <details> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary> ``` Treat finding text, fi\n42\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t64\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269356\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bulk relation mutations atomic** When one source in a bulk link operation fails or returns `{ ok: false }`, the other `Promise.all` mutations may already have committed before `assertMutationSucceeded` throws. The UI then reports the whole operation as failed even though some records were linked, and retrying can encounter duplicates; use a transactional batch mutation or compensate the successful mutations before propagating the failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n43\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t137\t2026-08-30T23:23:45Z\tpullfrog\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890834875\t`datafn.transact` bypasses DataFn's local/offline mutation path and always invokes the remote adapter. Local-only accounts and offline cloud sessions configure no remote adapter, so add-to-collection and bulk-link actions now throw instead of updating local storage. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve relation actions without a remote transport ## Affected sites - `client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts:137` calls the remote-only transaction API for every runtime mode. - `client/stores/datafn.store.ts:668` configures local and offline runtimes with `{ mode: \"local-only\" }` and no remote. - `@datafn/client` 0.1.0 implements `transact` through `remote.transact`\n44\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t159\t2026-08-31T00:34:07Z\tcoderabbitai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890996684\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_ <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary> 🏁 Script executed: ```shell #!/bin/bash set -eu printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable conventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- target file ---' cat -n client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts | sed -n '90,180p' printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct DataFn bindings and package version ---' rg -n --glob '!*node_modules*' 'from [\"'\\\\'']`@datafn/client`|datafn\\\\.mutate|datafn\\\\.transact' client shared package.json pnpm-lock.yaml yarn.lock package-lock.json 2>/dev/null | head -160 ``` Repository: 21nCo/nucleum Length of\n45\tclient/stores/datafn-sharing.store.test.ts\t129\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206098\t<!-- cubic:v=10a6b2a5-d027-4766-b799-5e3c517d828a --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P3: The mock runtime is installed with `datafnRuntime.set(runtime)` and only cleared by the final `datafnRuntime.set(null)` assertion-line statement, not by a teardown. If `createDatafnPublicLink` or an assertion throws, the mock stays installed on this module-level singleton, so any later test that resolves `resolveShareTable`/`resolvePublicLinksClient` silently gets the stale mock. Move the reset into `afterEach` (or a `try/finally`) so the shared store is always restored. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if t\n46\tclient/stores/datafn.store.test.ts\t182\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t648858933a\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206100\t<!-- cubic:v=f54633e3-8e80-4f85-b301-5b5ab1b568c6 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: The \"uses sync mode only for authenticated user spaces\" test never asserts the positive sync path. It only checks three local-only cases, so it would still pass if resolveDatafnMode stopped returning \"sync\" entirely. Add an assertion for CLOUD + userId + isOffline:false resolving to \"sync\" (and optionally isOfflinabilityEnabled:false to \"sync-direct\") to actually validate the behavior the title claims. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At c\n47\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t375\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827045\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve sync-direct writes across offline transitions** When a cloud user has disabled offlinability, a manual or network outage still takes this unconditional branch and opens a new, initially empty local-only database. Edits made there cannot clone up because the runtime is local-only; on reconnect, initialization returns to `sync-direct` and deletes that retired database, silently discarding those edits. Keep sync-direct read-only while offline, prevent this transition, or upload the temporary clone before deleting it. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2d59\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a055b1-b0ee-7061-8828-4da29bf187dc","create_time":1788144857.457619}}}
