{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:02:51.392Z","ordinal":9056,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a055c5-0900-7f31-ba62-bc6947d0c3c5","call_id":"call_qSBvVfOekKMPaoYzw4SGcMke","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"52-\n53-### keywords\n54-\n55:- SKI-6, McpFn, @mcpfn/auth@0.0.2, @mcpfn/core@0.0.2, @mcpfn/testing@0.0.2, pnpm mcpfn:verify, reviewThreads, PR #7, f9bc1d86, 4754f954\n56-\n57-## Task 2: Review SKI-13 multi-region implementation against specification, partial\n58-\n--\n73-## Reusable knowledge\n74-\n75-- Skillplane now consumes published `@mcpfn/auth`, `@mcpfn/core`, and `@mcpfn/testing` at `0.0.2`; remove local `link:` dependencies and `mcpfn-source.json`. McpFn owns runtime/MCP-specific authorization compatibility; AuthFn owns identity, sessions, consent, signing and durable security state; Skillplane owns tenancy, grants, approval, policy and tool behavior. PR #7 merged at exact head `f9bc1d86` as `4754f954`. [Task 1]\n76:- Start PR triage with unresolved GraphQL `reviewThreads`, then use review bodies, issue comments, and inline comments as supplemental evidence. Validate every finding in the exact-head worktree and stop after the bounded authorized round. [Task 1]\n77-- Multi-region correctness requires physical ownership and end-to-end paths, not only types/builds: regional code must not join global `workspaces`/memberships/service principals; trusted routed workspace identity must reach API context; public-by-ID/download/amendment routes must classify correctly; projection outbox consumers and transactionally enqueued events must exist; migration/deployment/runtime AuthFn paths must be concrete. [Task 2]\n78-\n79-## Failures and how to do differently\n--\n93-\n94-### keywords\n95-\n96:- splane pr-review-fix, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #567, PR #568, 69723719, 9c576dc, 41e1efbb, reviewThreads, legacy-product-keys, svelte-check\n97-\n98-## Task 2: Review DataFn field builders and implement PR #568 SearchFn configuration integrity, partial\n99-\n--\n355-- Symptom: CI has 5-second auth-test timeouts with `CONNECT_TIMEOUT ...:5432`. Cause: an unmocked new helper side effect escaped a unit test into staging RDS. Fix: mock `@/server/services/org-widgets/ensureHomeMasters` in every affected suite; do not relabel this as OOM/Docker/compiler failure or mask it by rerunning. [Task 2]\n356-- Symptom: Prettier/full unit tests report failures during a read-only review. Fix: compare the exact `HEAD` files and preserve precise baseline attribution; do not format just to silence pre-existing drift. [Task 1]\n357-\n358:# Task Group: August 29 Nucleus TIDY-442 review planning and immutable Diffpanel publication\n359-scope: Use to assess a broad Nucleus migration's dependency-safe review boundaries or publish a fresh immutable Diffpanel review for an exact live PR range.\n360-applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus; reuse_rule=the stack boundaries and safety mechanics are reusable, but branch divergence, file counts, paths, and `file:` dependency state require live revalidation.\n361-\n362:## Task 1: Assess the entire TIDY-442 changeset for easy reviews, partial\n363-\n364-### rollout_summary_files\n365-\n--\n367-\n368-### keywords\n369-\n370:- TIDY-442, stacked PRs, DataFn, Flux, origin/dev, datafn-migration-inventory.md, file: dependencies, extension/clipper, Playwright, git add -p\n371-\n372-## Task 2: Publish immutable Diffpanel chapters for PR #568, success\n373-\n--\n486-\n487-### keywords\n488-\n489:- MCP-2, McpFn, work-linear-issue@1.0.1, oauth-core 0.0.2, tsup, ESM, CommonJS, gate:mcpfn-release, reviewThreads, force-with-lease, PR-122, UNSTABLE\n490-\n491-## User preferences\n492-\n--\n900-\n901-### keywords\n902-\n903:- splane pr-review-fix, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #3, SKI-1, d398cba6, reviewThreads, outdated, repeatable-read, applicationCommit\n904-\n905-## Task 2: Explain GitHub-native stack and refresh PR #3/#5 status, success\n906-\n--\n992-\n993-### keywords\n994-\n995:- PR #116, SFNS-2, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, reviewThreads, nodeType, undefined versus null, authfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt, MCPFn, UIFn, d27cceb2\n996-\n997-## User preferences\n998-\n--\n1072-\n1073-### keywords\n1074-\n1075:- DEV-1, splane, 21n/work-linear-issue@1.0.1, next, DEV-1-origin-dev, devfn, Turbo, Node 22, PR #117, ff824c61, reviewThreads, bounded remediation, merged into dev\n1076-\n1077-## User preferences\n1078-\n--\n2121-\n2122-### keywords\n2123-\n2124:- PR #103, SF-8, `21n/report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`, `reviewThreads`, GraphQL, Outlook SSRF, checkpoint null, Python rate limit, `0cea01c4`, `git push origin HEAD:SF-8`\n2125-\n2126-## User preferences\n2127-\n--\n2135-- Package releases require package-local install/build/test/pack and dependency-safe batches. Failed immutable `@plugfn/providers@0.0.1` required corrected `0.0.2`; do not reuse failed tags. [Task 2]\n2136-- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\n2137-- Worktree snapshots are cache-relative without fetch; take final counts after detailed inspection if a checkout changes concurrently. [Task 3]\n2138:- For private Superfunctions PRs, inspect authenticated current `reviewThreads`/head comments, including `isResolved` and `isOutdated`, before editing. PR #103 used a clean isolated exact-head worktree because the existing checkout was dirty; after user authorization, fetch `origin/SF-8`, require it to equal `HEAD^`, then push `HEAD:SF-8` and verify local/remote/live PR SHA equality. [Task 4]\n2139-\n2140-## Failures and how to do differently\n2141-\n2142-- Passing focused PR tests missed `resolveScope()` precedence; external billing/CI gaps are separate from code correctness. [Task 1]\n2143-- Do not dispatch all tag releases sharing one concurrency group. Remove sibling-source aliases and root-tool assumptions from package tests; do not attribute generic JavaScript, Python, Vercel, or dependency-cycle baseline failures to McpFn without the exact job logs. [Task 2]\n2144:- A malformed GraphQL query can fail; use paginated `reviewThreads(first:100, after:$cursor)` and check `pageInfo.hasNextPage`. If `python` is absent from PATH, use the bundled runtime via a temporary `python` symlink before running `node scripts/ci-run-python-package.mjs plugfn/python`; keep full-repository baseline failures separate from changed-surface tests. [Task 4]\n2145-\n2146-# Task Group: August 11 btnextjs and btnextjs-two review/fix work in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/repos\n2147-scope: Use for exact-snapshot read-only review, subsequently authorized narrow fixes, and current CI attribution in btnextjs repositories.\n--\n2238-\n2239-### keywords\n2240-\n2241:- splane, 21n/report-and-fix-pr, PR #93, BillFn, GraphQL reviewThreads, package-lock.json, Kysely, memory adapter, `gh pr merge 93 --merge`\n2242-\n2243-## Task 2: PR #112 ExtFn review refetch, fixes, and push, success\n2244-\n--\n2248-\n2249-### keywords\n2250-\n2251:- PR #112, ExtFn, reviewThreads, unresolved threads, e7b4853f, 73 tests, billing lock\n2252-\n2253-## Task 3: ApiFn PR #113 refetch, remediation, and ready-for-review, success\n2254-\n--\n2258-\n2259-### keywords\n2260-\n2261:- PR #113, ApiFn, reviewThreads, TS5055, .svelte.d.ts, gh pr ready, faea2d04, unresolvedCount:0\n2262-\n2263-## Task 4: Remediate Superfunctions PR #103 locally through the hosted Skillplane workflow, success\n2264-\n--\n2268-\n2269-### keywords\n2270-\n2271:- PR #103, 21n/report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0, SF-8-ci-fixes, reviewThreads, 46 unique findings, Ruff, mypy, PlugFn, 236 review threads, delivery claim token\n2272-\n2273-## Task 5: Preserve dirty `next`, sync `sf-next/next`, and remediate MDFN PR #43, success\n2274-\n--\n2301-\n2302-## Reusable knowledge\n2303-\n2304:- Related skill: skills/thread-aware-pr-review-triage/SKILL.md. Collect PR metadata, pagination-complete inline comments, submitted reviews, conversation comments, and GraphQL `reviewThreads` before edits; collapse threads into current valid findings and mark stale ones separately. [Task 1][Task 3][Task 6]\n2305-- Quote `gh api` endpoint URLs containing `?` in zsh. Preview ignored generated siblings with `git clean -ndX <path>` before targeted cleanup; stale compiled JS can make Vitest exercise old code. For a large root lockfile conflict, select a coherent side then regenerate with `npm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts`; resolve adapter conflicts semantically and rerun focused DB/BillFn/Apple/Python gates before merging. [Task 1]\n2306-- CI blocked by a GitHub billing/account lock is neither a passing nor a demonstrated code failure; retain it as an external verification gap. [Task 2][Task 3]\n2307-- For hosted `splane PR fixes`, retrieve the exact live skill, work at the exact PR head in a dedicated worktree, gather all review surfaces before source edits, validate the report first, leave changes unstaged/uncommitted when required, then refetch reviews. PR #103 validated core `192`, providers `115`, and Python `66` tests plus TypeScript/Ruff/mypy/diff checks; repository-wide ESLint/Black remained baseline debt. [Task 4]\n2308-- Safe `next` synchronization: inspect status/remotes/worktrees; create preservation worktree from current local `next`; stash `--include-untracked`; apply `--index`; compare status/diff/index/untracked fingerprints; `git pull --ff-only sf-next next`; drop transfer stash only after equality verification. [Task 5]\n2309-- MDFN uses Markdown as canonical state with structured document, selection, diagnostics, history, and editorial sidecar; its framework-neutral kernel follows UIFn’s core -> DOM -> adapter-kit -> React/Svelte/Solid pattern. `npm run verify:mdfn` is the broad authoritative gate. [Task 5]\n2310-- For Superfunctions admin inventory, inspect tracked `*fn` packages directly because the root README is incomplete. `uifn/sf` has backed panels for AuthFn, PlugFn, FileFn, and BillFn; re-inventory tracked `*fn` directories before relying on the 35-product snapshot. [Task 6]\n2311:- PR #44 triage should fetch GraphQL `reviewThreads(first:100)` plus submitted reviews, issue comments, and inline comments, then separate current from outdated findings. The validated fixes were canonical `installationId`/deprecated `organizationId` handling, URI-encoded route-placeholder materialization in `AdminClient`, and direct-service rejection of undeclared WatchFn filters. [Task 6]\n2312-\n2313-## Failures and how to do differently\n2314-\n--\n3721-\n3722-### keywords\n3723-\n3724:- SKI-6, McpFn, @mcpfn/core@0.0.2, pnpm mcpfn:verify, reviewThreads, PR #7, f9bc1d86, 4754f954\n3725-\n3726-## Task 13: Ideate Skillplane local/cloud distribution and hybrid projections, partial\n3727-\n--\n4346-\n4347-### keywords\n4348-\n4349:- kgqa, PR 88, service_request, raw_service_response, is_raw_service_response, service_raw_answer, reviewThreads, gh api graphql, uv run pytest\n4350-\n4351-## Task 2: Fix data_analyst_agent PR 125 response-contract schema locally, success\n4352-\nworktree /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus\nHEAD bc10a13749a5be4bfd47bdebf67df05018df7718\nbranch refs/heads/codex/backup-tidy-442-unsplit-20260829\n\nworktree /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-568-review\nHEAD 9c576dc49b81473ccd3c6624610d68197384c0ed\nbranch refs/heads/codex/tidy-442-02-datafn-foundations\n\nworktree /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-569-review\nHEAD 49d13ae6bcfeac63fd129423163ba7220a2e2401\nbranch refs/heads/codex/tidy-442-03-account-runtime\n\nworktree /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-570-review\nHEAD 2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89\nbranch refs/heads/codex/tidy-442-04-client-runtime-auth\n\nwor