2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t236\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891447086\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove newly added inline documentation comments** This commit introduces numerous JSDoc and inline comments throughout the new migration code, with this block being one representative instance, even though repository policy requires edited code to remain comment-free. Remove the newly added code comments or move essential documentation outside the source files before merge. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L15-L16](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89/AGENTS.md#L15-L16) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n3891447088\tchatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\t2026-08-31T03:08:49Z\t2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89\tclient/stores/appMenu/appMenu.store.ts\t74\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891447088\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Roll back failed app-menu preference mutations** When `datafn.kv.merge()` rejects or resolves with `{ ok: false }`—for example, in `sync-direct` mode during a transient remote failure—this method has already updated `appMenuLocal` and never checks or rolls back the mutation. Pinning, unpinning, or reordering menu items consequently appears successful but disappears on the next authoritative signal or reload; handle the result and restore authoritative/pending state as the other migrated preference stores do. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89/AGENTS.md#L12-L13) Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n3891454716\tpullfrog[bot]\t2026-08-31T03:11:22Z\t2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t31\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891454716\tAn E2EE session can arrive from another device while this browser still has `DATAFN_OFFLINABILITY=\"false\"`. DataFn forces that session onto local storage, but disabling this switch without correcting the persisted flag leaves `resolveStoredAuthSessionState()` treating the device as non-offlinable, so the next offline launch rejects its cached cloud session. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Keep E2EE offlinability and cached-session auth consistent ## Affected sites - `client/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte:31` — disables the only UI control that could change the stale local flag. - `client/stores/datafn.store.ts:624-629` — forces E2EE onto storage-backed mode without persisting the effective offlinability value. - `client/components/account/auth.ts:208-221` — rejects cached cloud sessions whenever the stored flag remains `false`. ## Required outcome - When E2EE requires local storage, persist or otherwise expose that effective state to cached-session auth before an offline launch. - Render the disabled switch as enabled and cover the `stored false + remote E2EE + offline restart` path with a regression test. ```` </details>\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"NEW REVIEWS\n5062828172\tchatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\tCOMMENTED\t2026-08-31T03:08:49Z\t2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#pullrequestreview-5062828172\t ### 💡 Codex Review https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/2e46d625da43431cf0ce1e9cfd3812a7d3d9fa89/client/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte#L87-L92 **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Await DataFn backup delivery before reporting success** In the separate regular DataFn backup path for an embedded iOS/macOS app, `downloadFromBlob()` asynchronously uploads and hands off the backup and can reject or return `false`, but this call is not awaited or checked before the success toast at lines 93–94. A failed upload is therefore reported as a succ