{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:13:23.935Z","ordinal":9213,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a053e7-239f-7703-8a5b-d9d8ac22d6de","turn_id":"01a055c4-948d-7b90-8dbf-b059d8086b3b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a1fc1bd5-3879-4912-b063-e850a1b05087","process_id":"35025","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-2e46d625.tedGCp\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \"\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \"\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \"\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \"\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[0:15][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\"[\\\\r\\\\n]+\";\" \")|.[0:520])] | @tsv' \"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\""],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus-pr-570-review","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr570-review-snapshot-2e46d625.tedGCp\njq -r '[.[] | select(.isResolved == false) | .comments.nodes[-1] as $c | {path:(.path // $c.path // \"\"), line:(.line // $c.line // .originalLine // $c.originalLine // 0), createdAt:$c.createdAt, author:($c.author.login // \"\"), commit:($c.commit.oid // \"\"), outdated:$c.outdated, url:($c.url // \"\"), body:$c.body}] | sort_by(.path,.line,.createdAt) | to_entries | .[0:15][] | [.key, .value.path, (.value.line|tostring), .value.createdAt, .value.author, (.value.commit[0:10]), (.value.outdated|tostring), .value.url, (.value.body|gsub(\"[\\\\r\\\\n]+\";\" \")|.[0:520])] | @tsv' \"$snapshot_dir/threads.json\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"0\tclient/components/account/auth.ts\t238\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions** For users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to \n1\tclient/components/record/recent.store.ts\t128\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table** For Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \"search\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compa\n2\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t66\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122431\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode** When a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude `sync-direct` here o\n3\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t120\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827057\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid clone-up for local-only restores** When an offline-only account or a cloud account currently in offline mode restores a backup, this always requests `triggerCloneUp` even though the active runtime has no remote transport. The import can therefore fail after writing local rows, leaving the UI reporting failure with a partially restored database; the legacy recovery path already avoids this by enabling clone-up only when `ru\n4\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t293\t2026-08-31T02:55:45Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891407784\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Await delivery before reporting a legacy backup** In an embedded iOS or macOS settings flow, `downloadFromBlob()` performs an asynchronous native upload/handoff and can reject or return `false`, but this newly added path does not await it and immediately shows the success toast. Although the startup recovery path now validates the same helper, a failed manual legacy backup is still reported as delivered and produces an unhandled\n5\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t29\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122432\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Recompute network state after reconnecting** If Sync Settings is mounted while the browser is offline and then the connection returns, `isNetworkInducedOfflineMode` remains the mount-time value `true`. Although `BaseLayer` updates `$context.isInOfflineMode` to false, this new toggle therefore stays disabled until the settings component is remounted, preventing the user from changing offline availability after reconnecting. Deriv\n6\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t31\t2026-08-31T03:11:22Z\tpullfrog\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891454716\tAn E2EE session can arrive from another device while this browser still has `DATAFN_OFFLINABILITY=\"false\"`. DataFn forces that session onto local storage, but disabling this switch without correcting the persisted flag leaves `resolveStoredAuthSessionState()` treating the device as non-offlinable, so the next offline launch rejects its cached cloud session. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Keep E2EE offlinability and cached-session auth consistent ## Affected sites - `client/components/s\n7\tclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t81\t2026-08-30T22:59:12Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890782302\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Delete the local clone when disabling offlinability** When a sync user turns off “Keep data available offline,” this initialization only closes the current adapter and switches to `sync-direct`; neither this handler nor the runtime teardown deletes or clears the retired IndexedDB database. The device therefore retains the user's complete local clone indefinitely despite the setting promising that no local copy is kept; after pen\n8\tclient/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\t186\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206015\t<!-- cubic:v=192b913b-f3f8-4c32-bbaa-410bc61d68cf --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} --> P1: Existing calendar, task, and analytics callers still read `greaterThanOrEqual`/`lessThanOrEqual`, so this new shape supplies them undefined bounds and breaks filtering. Preserve the legacy keys until callers are migrated, or update every caller to `$gte`/`$lte`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, unde\n9\tclient/components/settings/timezone/tz.store.ts\t298\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269353\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply the historical timezone correction instead of a round trip** When a Pointron user has timezone-change records, `AnalyticsCardView` and `AnalyticsChartStandalone` depend on this method to normalize historical session timestamps. Resolving date parts in a timezone and immediately resolving those same parts back in the same timezone returns the original instant, so the correction is effectively a no-op and sessions can be gro\n10\tclient/components/settings/userPreferences.store.ts\t128\t2026-08-31T02:10:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891265052\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore writable updates for preference bindings** Svelte compiles assignments and bindings such as those in `SizeFactorSetting`, `AppearanceSettings`, `DateTimeSettings`, and `CmdResults` into calls to `userPreferences.set(...)`, but this replacement exposes only `subscribe`, `get`, and `modify`. When users change sizing, popup blur, time scales, day-start values, or recent commands, the generated handler therefore fails instea\n11\tclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t48\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827049\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore the Nucleum entitlement gate after authentication** For cloud users opening the Nucleum product, this replacement admits every successful session without the prior `account.ping()` and `PlanType.NUCLEUS` check. A repo-wide search finds no remaining navigation to `/error/access-denied`, and AuthFn session resolution does not populate or enforce the account plan, so users with only a Memotron or Pointron entitlement can en\n12\tclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t92\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075826\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow cached Nucleum sessions to use their offline clone** When a Nucleum cloud user with offlinability enabled launches during a network outage or manual offline mode, `resolveAuthSession()` deliberately returns `cached-cloud`, but this branch unconditionally sends them to access denied without consulting any cached entitlement. Unlike the prior gate, which only denied a known non-Nucleum plan, this locks every entitled Nucleum\n13\tclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t178\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122427\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the cached plan when entitlement refresh fails** When an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the plan endpoint is temporarily unavailable, the account update immediately above has already cleared the cached plan and this condition treats the missing response as a failed entitlement. Entitled Nucleum users are consequently redirected to access denied despite the newly persiste\n14\tclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t461\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269351\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve manual offline mode across connectivity events** When a user has explicitly enabled offline mode and the browser reconnects, this handler derives `isOffline` solely from `navigator.onLine`, overwrites the stored-mode state, and switches DataFn back to sync. The reconnect can therefore upload locally queued changes despite the user's offline-mode selection; combine network state with `ClientStorageKey.OFFLINE_MODE` befor\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"0\tclient/components/account/auth.ts\t238\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions** For users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to \n1\tclient/components/record/recent.store.ts\t128\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table** For Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \"search\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compa\n2\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t66\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t03838922