When an active AuthFn session is valid but `refreshPlanData()` returns `undefined` because the plan endpoint is temporarily unavailable, the account update immediately above has already cleared the cached plan and this condition treats the missing response as a failed entitlement. Entitled Nucleum users are consequently redirected to access denied despite the newly persiste\n14\tclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t461\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269351\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve manual offline mode across connectivity events** When a user has explicitly enabled offline mode and the browser reconnects, this handler derives `isOffline` solely from `navigator.onLine`, overwrites the stored-mode state, and switches DataFn back to sync. The reconnect can therefore upload locally queued changes despite the user's offline-mode selection; combine network state with `ClientStorageKey.OFFLINE_MODE` befor\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3125},"formatted_output":"0\tclient/components/account/auth.ts\t238\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201426\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove stale offline markers when expiring cloud sessions** For users migrated from the previous runtime, cloud identity commonly coexists with `OFFLINE_SESSION_ID` because the old sign-in flow created that marker. On a confirmed expired AuthFn session, this cleanup removes every cloud marker but leaves the offline ID; the next session resolution therefore classifies the same browser as `offline-only`, allowing a later visit to \n1\tclient/components/record/recent.store.ts\t128\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122429\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map combination recents to the space table** For Memotron and Nucleum, `resolveProductResources(..., \"search\")` still supplies `Resource.combination`, but the DataFn schema defines the renamed table as `space`. This code therefore queries the nonexistent `combination` table; `refresh()` catches the error per resource, so recently updated spaces silently disappear from the recents UI. Apply the same `combination`-to-`space` compa\n2\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t66\t2026-08-31T01:19:42Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0383892256\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891122431\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode** When a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude `sync-direct` here o\n3\tclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t120\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827057\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid clone-up for local-only restores** When an offline-only account or a cloud account currently in offline mode restores a backup, this always requests `triggerCloneUp` even though the active runtime has no remote transport. The import can therefore fail after writing local rows, leaving the UI reporting failure with a partially restored database; the legacy recovery path already avoids this by enabling clone-up only when `ru\n4\tclient/components/settings