mplement IndexedDB but not `indexedDB.databases()`, this returns `undefined`, causing `detectLegacyLocalData()` to report `isSupported: false`; `UserBaseLayer` then skips the recovery gate and starts with an empty DataFn database even though the active user's legacy `${userId}-1` or `${dapId}-1` database is still present. Probe the d\n29\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1044\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210782\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Rehydrate binary values during legacy import** For legacy `file` records containing `Uint8Array`, `ArrayBuffer`, Blob, or File data, export replaces the bytes with a `__legacyIndexedDbType`/`dataBase64` marker, but this fallback imports that marker as a plain object instead of decoding it. The unchanged file consumers expect `Uint8Array` data, so recovered offline attachments and thumbnails become empty or unreadable even though\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5042},"formatted_output":"15\tclient/layout/layers/BaseLayer.svelte\t609\t2026-08-29T09:53:58Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206027\t<!-- cubic:v=74adb245-1155-4663-8f26-acad72481976 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P2: Removing this `<span id=\"global-sync-status\">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById(\"global-sync-status\")?.getAttribute(\"data-syncstatus\")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefine\n16\tclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t176\t2026-08-30T23:51:05Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t9aadca2ea9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890895070\t*