es paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"30\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1120\t2026-08-31T02:55:45Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891407770\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map legacy children before schema filtering** When a Memotron or Nucleum backup contains legacy `node.children`, this whitelist drops the field because the DataFn schema exposes only `mdChildOrder`, while `transformLegacyRecord()` has no node conversion. The separate `migrateDatafnNodeMdChildOrder()` pass runs before the recovery import and records its completion marker, so recovered markdown nodes permanently lose their ordered\n31\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1191\t2026-08-31T02:55:45Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891407778\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Populate required objective defaults for PointGoal rows** For old Pointron `PointGoal` rows, the retained `IPointGoal` shape has no `type` or `status` fields and instead may contain `isCompleted`, but this conversion only handles ancestry and layout. Both fields are required by the DataFn objective schema, so these rows are rejected as skipped and the startup recovery cannot complete; synthesize the historical defaults and trans\n32\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1233\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t91a40ab57f\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075834\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve Po