/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map goal collection searches to objective** When “Add item to collection” is used for a Pointron goal collection or a goal-typed Nucleum collection, `Collection.svelte` passes the legacy `goal` resource here, but the DataFn schema exposes that resource as `objective`. Forwarding `goal` to `datafn.search()` makes non-empty searches fail or return no goals, even though the blank-query recents path has a compatibility mapping; tran\n44\tclient/stores/app.store.ts\t207\t2026-08-31T02:28:18Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tfa3b44579e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891321878\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain the legacy goal route in the mobile menu gate** On portrait layouts, breadcrumb navigation still calls `gotoResource()` with legacy resource IDs and therefore produces paths such as `/goal/goal:...`. Replacing the matcher with only `/objective/*` makes `checkIfNeedToHideMenu()` return false for those goal detail routes, leaving the app menu visible where it was previously hidden; retain `/goal/*` until all route producers\n"},"started_at_ms":1788146017333,"completed_at_ms":1788146017333}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:13:37.354Z","ordinal":9224,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a055ce-e44a-7951-82d1-58aa621a17e9","call_id":"call_N8wcr6NuHqjCmdT7epIxMnyb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"30\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1120\t2026-08-31T02:55:45Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891407770\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map legacy children before schema filtering** When a Memotron or Nucleum backup contains legacy `node.children`, this whitelist drops the field because the DataFn schema exposes only `mdChildOrder`, while `transformLegacyRecord()` has no node conversion. The separate `migrateDatafnNodeMdChildOrder()` pass runs before the recovery import and records its completion marker, so recovered markdown nodes permanently lose their ordered\n31\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1191\t2026-08-31T02:55:45Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891407778\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Populate required objective defaults for PointGoal rows** For old Pointron `PointGoal` rows, the retained `IPointGoal` shape has no `type` or `status` fields and instead may contain `isCompleted`, but this conversion only handles ancestry and layout. Both fields are required by the DataFn objective schema, so these rows are rejected as skipped and the startup recovery cannot complete; synthesize the historical defaults and trans\n32\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1233\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t91a40ab57f\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075834\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve PointLog rows that predate session IDs** For legacy Pointron `PointLog` rows created before sessions were attached, `sessionId` is absent—the retained legacy `FocusLog` type still declares it optional—so this conversion silently drops otherwise valid `start`, `totalFocus`, and `totalBreak` history. Recovery then records a successful decision and suppresses future prompts because these pre-import omissions are not report\n33\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1241\t2026-08-31T01:28:47Z\tpullfrog\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891146946\tSessionless `PointLog` rows now receive a `sessionId`, but the import payload never creates the corresponding `session`. The remote schema enforces this required foreign key, and legacy streak rows concretely omit `sessionId`, so their recovery can fail instead of preserving them. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve sessionless PointLog rows without orphaned references ## Affected sites - `client/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts:1233-1235` — invents a session foreign key withou\n34\tclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1248\t2026-08-31T01:56:04Z\tpullfrog\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891224029\tThe exact sessionless rows cited by the original finding are created with `goalId: \"PointGoal:Empty\"`, but no matching goal exists. This converts that sentinel to `objective:Empty`, and the generated remote schema enforces `sessionLog.objectiveId` as a foreign key, so creating the synthetic session only moves the import failure to this relation. Drop the sentinel objective reference or create a matching supported resource, and add the exact streak-row fixture to verify the complete payload.\n35\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t420\t2026-08-29T09:51:56Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886201425\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clear DataFn data before destroying the runtime** When AuthFn account deletion succeeds, `signOut()` first calls `destroyNucleumDatafn()`, which clears `runtimeStore`; the following `clearDatafnLocalData()` immediately returns because there is no `runtime?.storage`. Consequently, deleting an account leaves its IndexedDB cache and user data on the device. Clear the active storage before signing out, or retain the storage handle t\n36\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t2026-08-31T01:52:23Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\tce677ed4a4\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891213268\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject failed DataFn file metadata mutations** When an S3 upload succeeds but the following DataFn mutation resolves with `{ ok: false }`, this code ignores the result and returns `[file]` as though persistence succeeded. Callers such as `MediaGrid.uploadToS3()` then retain the returned file reference even though no file record exists, producing broken attachments; inspect the mutation result and propagate its error before retur\n37\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t2026-08-31T02:55:45Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891407781\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Read uploaded file metadata from DataFn** For normal cloud uploads, this saves file metadata only through DataFn, but `fileStore` still extends the Flux-backed `ResourceStore`; consumers such as `DraggableMediaGridElement` later resolve saved IDs with `fileStore.refresh()`. The object supplied immediately after upload therefore renders initially, but after reopening or reloading the document the Flux lookup has no corresponding \n38\tclient/stores/account.store.ts\t883\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\tce677ed4a4\ttru