ussion_r3890231197\t_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_ **Remove dead commented-out code in the modified files.** Delete the inactive statement, declaration, and render block in `app.store.ts`, `userPreferences.store.ts`, and `UserLayout.svelte`. Keep any future behavior changes in a tracked follow-up rather than leaving disabled production code beside the active implementation. <details> <summary>📍 Affects 3 files</summary> - `client/stores/app.store.ts#L700-L700` (this comment) - `client/components/setti\n46\tclient/stores/appMenu/appMenu.store.ts\t74\t2026-08-31T03:08:49Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891447088\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Roll back failed app-menu preference mutations** When `datafn.kv.merge()` rejects or resolves with `{ ok: false }`—for example, in `sync-direct` mode during a transient remote failure—this method has already updated `appMenuLocal` and never checks or rolls back the mutation. Pinning, unpinning, or reordering menu items consequently appears successful but disappears on the next authoritative signal or reload; handle the result an\n47\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t64\t2026-08-30T19:08:22Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t589009fcb9\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890269356\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bulk relation mutations atomic** When one source in a bulk link operation fails or returns `{ ok: false }`, the other `Promise.all` mutations may already have committed before `assertMutationSucceeded` throws. The UI then reports the whole operation as failed even though some records were linked, and retrying can encounter duplicates; use a transactional batch mutation or compensate the successful mutations before propagati\n48\tclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t137\t2026-08-30T23:23:45Z\tpullfrog\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890834875\t`datafn.transact` bypasses DataFn's local/offline mutation path and always invokes the remote adapter. Local-only accounts and offline cloud sessions configure no remote adapter, so add-to-collection and bulk-link actions now throw instead of updating local storage. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve relation actions without a remote transport ## Affected sites - `client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts:137` calls the remote-only transaction API for every runtime mode. - `client/sto\n49\tclient/stores/datafn-sharing.store.test.ts\t129\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206098\t<!-- cubic:v=10a6b2a5-d027-4766-b799-5e3c517d828a --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} --> P3: The mock runtime is installed with `datafnRuntime.set(runtime)` and only cleared by the final `datafnRuntime.set(null)` assertion-line statement, not by a teardown. If `createDatafnPublicLink` or an assertion throws, the mock stays installed on this module-level singleton, so any later test that resolves `resolveShareTable`/`resolvePublicLinksClient` silently ge\n50\tclient/stores/datafn.store.test.ts\t182\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206100\t<!-- cubic:v=f54633e3-8e80-4f85-b301-5b5ab1b568c6 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: The \"uses sync mode only for authenticated user spaces\" test never asserts the positive sync path. It only checks three local-only cases, so it would still pass if resolveDatafnMode stopped returning \"sync\" entirely. Add an assertion for CLOUD + userId + isOffline:false resolving to \"sync\" (and optionally isOfflinabilityEnabled:false to \"s