rdown. If `createDatafnPublicLink` or an assertion throws, the mock stays installed on this module-level singleton, so any later test that resolves `resolveShareTable`/`resolvePublicLinksClient` silently ge\n50\tclient/stores/datafn.store.test.ts\t182\t2026-08-29T09:53:59Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206100\t<!-- cubic:v=f54633e3-8e80-4f85-b301-5b5ab1b568c6 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} --> P3: The \"uses sync mode only for authenticated user spaces\" test never asserts the positive sync path. It only checks three local-only cases, so it would still pass if resolveDatafnMode stopped returning \"sync\" entirely. Add an assertion for CLOUD + userId + isOffline:false resolving to \"sync\" (and optionally isOfflinabilityEnabled:false to \"sync-direct\") to actuall\n51\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t236\t2026-08-31T03:08:49Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891447086\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Remove newly added inline documentation comments** This commit introduces numerous JSDoc and inline comments throughout the new migration code, with this block being one representative instance, even though repository policy requires edited code to remain comment-free. Remove the newly added code comments or move essential documentation outside the source files before merge. AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L15-L16](https://githu\n52\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t375\t2026-08-30T23:20:02Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2d59ba577b\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890827045\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve sync-direct writes across offline transitions** When a cloud user has disabled offlinability, a manual or network outage still takes this unconditional branch and opens a new, initially empty local-only database. Edits made there cannot clone up because the runtime is local-only; on reconnect, initialization returns to `sync-direct` and deletes that retired database, silently discarding those edits. Keep sync-direct rea\n53\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t537\t2026-08-30T18:42:30Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t0c1c83f24e\ttrue\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3890210778\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Abort startup when remote E2EE settings cannot be read** When an E2EE-enabled account starts on a new device without cached local settings and this metadata request fails transiently, converting the failure to `null` makes `resolveDatafnE2eeConfig()` treat encryption as disabled. Initialization then opens normal sync with `e2ee: null`, so the user cannot decrypt existing records and subsequent writes may be uploaded without the \n54\tclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t912\t2026-08-31T01:01:58Z\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3891075824\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore E2EE after a failed disable attempt** If writing the disabled metadata or `cloneUpAllDatafnData()` fails, this has already removed E2EE from the live client. The catch restores the old metadata and calls `initializeNucleumDatafn()`, but the runtime key still contains the same `keyRef`, so initialization returns the existing runtime without reinstalling its provider. Subsequent sync writes can therefore remain unencrypted\n55\tclient/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts\t246\t2026-08-29T09:53:57Z\tcubic-dev-ai\t2e46d625da\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/pull/570#discussion_r3886206001\t<!-- cubic:v=179c0b6e-949a-450a-a389-f69cb4a8d5c4 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P