hange the token, leaving the user on the login prompt. Allow the token-bearing route to mount `AuthGuard`, or exchange the embed token before resolving the route auth state.  <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agent\nclient/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts\t246\t<!-- cubic:v=179c0b6e-949a-450a-a389-f69cb4a8d5c4 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P1: When a user enables E2EE and then signs into a different account in the same browser, this global cache makes the new account reuse the previous account's DEK. Its runtime then encrypts and syncs new-account data without matching remote E2EE metadata, so other devices cannot unlock it; scope the settings/key cache by account namespace or clea\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t90\t<!-- cubic:v=2f29a7a1-713c-46af-8012-33deb997f3d5 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P1: If runtime reinitialization fails after the old runtime is destroyed, this catch restores the flag but not the DataFn runtime. Reinitialize the previous mode before reporting the failure.  <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>  ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At client/components\nclient/components/account/auth.ts\t0\t<!-- cubic:v=243a7019-7789-4e62-9931-0184e98b84a5 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} --> P1: During SSR, `resolveAuthSession()` now calls `determineIfOffline()` before its server guard. `determineIfOffline()` reads `navigator.onLine`, so Node rendering rejects instead of returning the intended signed-out state; make this call SSR-safe.  <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>  ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, \nclient/utils/network.utils.ts\t0\t<!-- cubic:v=e08d40c7-66de-4131-99f1-034b2a4e55ae --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-6322