agents</summary>  ```text Check if this issue \nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t0\t<!-- cubic:v=385d8f2a-e826-4da1-bab8-7310c9d8de19 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P1: When a device switches from an E2EE account to an account whose remote setting is disabled, this branch still selects the previous account's global local settings. Treat a present remote setting, including disabled settings, as authoritative or namespace local E2EE settings per account.  <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>  ```t\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t0\t<!-- cubic:v=09ebaedb-984e-4797-b9a7-549deb8397a7 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7522f186-2360-43cc-b9ce-632214bd3d94 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P1: When E2EE is enabled from `sync-direct`, the runtime switches to a new empty local store before replacing the remote clone. Pull the remote dataset into that store before cloning, or block E2EE enablement in direct mode until a safe migration path exists.  <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>  ```text Check if this issue is valid\nclient/stores/datafnE2ee.store.ts\t0\t<!-- cubic:v=1bee4dfc-f810-424b-b217-1c49d8166a2a --> <!-- cubic:review-run=9a7e6eac-b146-4340-9e2b-54409b395acb --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P1: Custom agent: **Flag Security Vulnerabilities**  When E2EE is enabled, this line persists the raw DEK as reversible base64 in `localStorage`/`chrome.storage.local`, and startup later auto-loads it without a password. A storage reader can therefore decrypt all DataFn payloads, bypassing the password wrapping. Keep the DEK only in memory or per\nclient/stores/uiState/uiState.type.ts\t38\t<!-- cubic:v=4a26eaff-5fd5-4573-ac72-296510e428ce --> <!-- cubic:review-run=9a7e6eac-b146-4340-9e2b-54409b395acb --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P1: Custom agent: **Check System Design and Architectural Patterns**  When existing UI state is stored under the old enum values, these r