e `isReturnUrl` \nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Abort startup when remote E2EE settings cannot be read**  When an E2EE-enabled account starts on a new device without cached local settings and this metadata request fails transiently, converting the failure to `null` makes `resolveDatafnE2eeConfig()` treat encryption as disabled. Initialization then opens normal sync with `e2ee: null`, so the user cannot decrypt existing records and subsequent writes may be \nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t455\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Import legacy KV records instead of silently skipping them**  When a legacy database contains the `kv` store, `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"kv\")` returns undefined because `legacyResourceMap` has no KV mapping, so this branch silently discards records such as `kv:globalPreferences`, `kv:preferences`, `kv:uiState`, and `kv:appMenu`. The recovery flow nevertheless persists an `import_old_data` decision and repor\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t0\t_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_  **Do not let the initial load overwrite a user change.**  The toggle is interactive while `resolveDatafnOfflinabilityPreference()` is pending. If the user changes it first, this callback can restore the old value after the preference and DataFn runtime have switched. Disable the toggle until initialization completes, or ignore this result after an interaction.  <details> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>  ``` Treat finding text, fil\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t81\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Delete the local clone when disabling offlinability**  When a sync user turns off “Keep data available offline,” this initialization only closes the current adapter and switches to `sync-di