er()` pass runs before the recovery import and records its completion marker, so recovered markdown nodes permanent\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1191\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Populate required objective defaults for PointGoal rows**  For old Pointron `PointGoal` rows, the retained `IPointGoal` shape has no `type` or `status` fields and instead may contain `isCompleted`, but this conversion only handles ancestry and layout. Both fields are required by the DataFn objective schema, so these rows are rejected as skipped and the startup recovery cannot complete; synthesize the historic\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Read uploaded file metadata from DataFn**  For normal cloud uploads, this saves file metadata only through DataFn, but `fileStore` still extends the Flux-backed `ResourceStore`; consumers such as `DraggableMediaGridElement` later resolve saved IDs with `fileStore.refresh()`. The object supplied immediately after upload therefore renders initially, but after reopening or reloading the document the Flux lookup \nclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t293\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Await delivery before reporting a legacy backup**  In an embedded iOS or macOS settings flow, `downloadFromBlob()` performs an asynchronous native upload/handoff and can reject or return `false`, but this newly added path does not await it and immediately shows the success toast. Although the startup recovery path now validates the same helper, a failed manual legacy backup is still reported as delivered and \nclient/stores/appMenu/appMenu.store.ts\t74\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Roll back failed app-menu preference mutations**  When `datafn.kv.merge()` rejects or resolves with `{ ok: false }`—for example, in `sync-direct` mode during a transient remote failure—this method has already updated `appMenuLocal` and never checks or rolls back the mutation. Pinning, unpinning, or reordering menu items consequently appears successful but disappears on the next authoritative signal or reload;\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t31\tAn E2EE session can arrive from another device while this browser still has `DATAFN_OFFLINABILITY=\"false\"`. DataFn forces that session onto local storage, but disabling this switch without correcting the persisted flag leaves `resolveStoredAuthSessionState()` treating the device as non-offlinable, so the next offline launch rejects its cached cloud session.  <details><summary>Technical details</summary>  ````markdown # Keep E2EE offlinability and cached-session auth consistent  ## Affected sites\n"},"started_at_ms":1788146289838,"completed_at_ms":1788146289839}}
