ove the `isReturnUrl` \nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Abort startup when remote E2EE settings cannot be read**  When an E2EE-enabled account starts on a new device without cached local settings and this metadata request fails transiently, converting the failure to `null` makes `resolveDatafnE2eeConfig()` treat encryption as disabled. Initialization then opens normal sync with `e2ee: null`, so the user cannot decrypt existing records and subsequent writes may be \nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t455\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Import legacy KV records instead of silently skipping them**  When a legacy database contains the `kv` store, `resolveLegacyStoreResource(\"kv\")` returns undefined because `legacyResourceMap` has no KV mapping, so this branch silently discards records such as `kv:globalPreferences`, `kv:preferences`, `kv:uiState`, and `kv:appMenu`. The recovery flow nevertheless persists an `import_old_data` decision and repor\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t0\t_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_  **Do not let the initial load overwrite a user change.**  The toggle is interactive while `resolveDatafnOfflinabilityPreference()` is pending. If the user changes it first, this callback can restore the old value after the preference and DataFn runtime have switched. Disable the toggle until initialization completes, or ignore this result after an interaction.  <details> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>  ``` Treat finding text, fil\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t81\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Delete the local clone when disabling offlinability**  When a sync user turns off “Keep data available offline,” this initialization only closes the current adapter and switches to `sync-direct`; neither this handler nor the runtime teardown deletes or clears the retired IndexedDB database. The device therefore retains the user's complete local clone indefinitely despite the setting promising that no local co\nclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t0\t_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_  <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>  🏁 Script executed:  ```shell printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable repository knowledge ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -maxdepth 2 -type f -name '*.md' -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- scoped guidance ---' for f in /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00/*/*.md; do   case \"$f\" in     *client*|*settings*|*data*|*svelte*) printf '\\\\n### %s\\\\n' \"\nclient/routes/(app)/+layout.svelte\t29\t_🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🔴 Critical_ | _⚡ Quick win_  <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>  🏁 Script executed:  ```shell #!/bin/bash # Confirm the `page` store import is absent in the (app) layout. fd -t f '\\\\+layout\\\\.svelte' client/routes | while read -r f; do   printf '\\\\n### %s\\\\n' \"$f\"   rg -n '\\\\$app/stores|\\\\$app/state|\\\\bpage\\\\b' \"$f\" done ```  Repository: 21nCo/nucleum  Length of output: 339  ---  🏁 Script executed:  ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e printf '%s\\\\n' '### a\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve sync-direct writes across offline transitions**  When a cloud user has disabled offlinability, a manual or network outage still takes this unconditional branch and opens a new, initially empty local-only database. Edits made there cannot clone up because the runtime is local-only; on reconnect, initialization returns to `sync-direct` and deletes that retired database, silently discarding those edits.\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t461\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Normalize renamed resource IDs during legacy import**  For imports from renamed stores such as `goal`, `PointGoal`, `todo`, `PointTask`, or `combination`, the target table is changed to `objective`, `task`, or `space`, but the record ID is retained verbatim here; the added tests even preserve `goal:*` IDs in objective rows. DataFn's `determineResourceType()` returns the ID prefix literally, so selecting a rec\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1240\t**P1: Keep migrated foreign keys aligned with target IDs**  The generic converter preserves imported `PointSession:*` and `PointGoal:*` record IDs, but this helper rewrites their references to `session:*` and `objective:*`; those targets do not exist, so server foreign-key checks reject the converted logs. Empty synthetic `PointLog` rows also lack a session and receive a fabricated one from the log ID; preserve exact references or remap target IDs consistently, and skip placeholder logs that hav\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t0\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_  <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>  🏁 Script executed:  ```shell #!/bin/bash # Description: Inspect legacy table configuration for overlapping store names mapped to one DataFn resource. set -euo pipefail  fd -t f 'product.config.ts|tableConfig|resource.store.ts' client | while IFS= read -r file; do   rg -n -C 4 \"PointGoal|PointTask|PointSession|PointLog|\\\\\"goal\\\\\"|\\\\\"todo\\\\\"\" \"$file\" || true done  rg -n -C 6 'leg\nclient/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts\t0\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_  <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>  🏁 Script executed:  ```shell #!/bin/bash set -eu printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable conventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- target file ---' cat -n client/stores/datafn-linking.store.ts | sed -n '90,180p' printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct DataFn bindings and package version ---' rg -n --glob '!*node_mod\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t912\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restore E2EE after a failed disable attempt**  If writing the disabled metadata or `cloneUpAllDatafnData()` fails, this has already removed E2EE from the live client. The catch restores the old metadata and calls `initializeNucleumDatafn()`, but the runtime key still contains the same `keyRef`, so initialization returns the existing runtime without reinstalling its provider. Subsequent sync writes can therefo\nclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t92\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Allow cached Nucleum sessions to use their offline clone**  When a Nucleum cloud user with offlinability enabled launches during a network outage or manual offline mode, `resolveAuthSession()` deliberately returns `cached-cloud`, but this branch unconditionally sends them to access denied without consulting any cached entitlement. Unlike the prior gate, which only denied a known non-Nucleum plan, this locks e\nclient/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte\t0\tRejecting every `cached-cloud` session blocks legitimate subscribed Nucleum users whenever they start offline or AuthFn has a retryable outage. `resolveAuthSession()` only emits this state for a stored cloud identity with DataFn offlinability enabled, so this redirect defeats the intended offline startup contract.  <details><summary>Technical details</summary>  ````markdown # Preserve Nucleum offline startup  ## Affected sites - `client/layout/layers/AuthGuard.svelte:84-89` — redirects all Nucle\nclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Disable E2EE setup in sync-direct mode**  When a cloud user has turned off “Keep data available offline,” the runtime is `sync-direct`, but this predicate enables the “Turn on E2EE” flow. After the user enters and confirms a password, `enableNucleumDatafnE2ee()` unconditionally rejects that mode with “Enable offline storage before turning on E2EE,” so the advertised operation can never succeed. Either exclude\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t920\tIf disabled metadata was written, clone-up fails, and this restore write also fails, the live context and local settings have already returned to E2EE while remote authority remains disabled. The next online initialization trusts that remote value and can open encrypted local data without a provider.  <details><summary>Technical details</summary>  ````markdown # Keep E2EE authorities consistent when disable rollback fails  ## Affected sites - `client/stores/datafn.store.ts:861-871` — commits dis\nclient/layout/layers/UserBaseLayer.svelte\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Confirm native backup delivery before suppressing recovery**  In an embedded iOS/macOS recovery flow, `downloadLegacyLocalBackup()` starts the asynchronous `fileStore.downloadFromBlob()` upload/handoff without awaiting or validating it, and this branch immediately saves `download_backup_continue`. If the upload fails or returns no URL, the UI still reports success and permanently suppresses the startup recove\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject failed DataFn file metadata mutations**  When an S3 upload succeeds but the following DataFn mutation resolves with `{ ok: false }`, this code ignores the result and returns `[file]` as though persistence succeeded. Callers such as `MediaGrid.uploadToS3()` then retain the returned file reference even though no file record exists, producing broken attachments; inspect the mutation result and propagate i\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t0\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject unavailable sessions in extension checks**  When AuthFn returns `unavailable` and the stored session is not eligible for cached-cloud use—for example, an extension has a bearer token but no cached `USER_INFO`, or offlinability is disabled—this returns `false`. `SheetBaseLayer.performSessionExpiryCheck()` and `ExtensionBaseLayer.checkIfSessionExpired()` interpret that as an active session and proceed to\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t0\tThe exact sessionless rows cited by the original finding are created with `goalId: \"PointGoal:Empty\"`, but no matching goal exists. This converts that sentinel to `objective:Empty`, and the generated remote schema enforces `sessionLog.objectiveId` as a foreign key, so creating the synthetic session only moves the import failure to this relation. Drop the sentinel objective reference or create a matching supported resource, and add the exact streak-row fixture to verify the complete payload.\nclient/stores/datafn.store.ts\t615\t_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_  <details> <summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>  🏁 Script executed:  ```shell #!/bin/bash set -e printf '%s\\\\n' '--- applicable repository conventions ---' find /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/21nco-nucleum-01ac9b00 -type f -name '*.md' -maxdepth 3 -print printf '%s\\\\n' '--- changed hunk ---' sed -n '540,630p' client/stores/datafn.store.ts printf '%s\\\\n' '--- direct definitions and calls ---' rg -n -C 4 'writeRemoteDatafnE2\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1120\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Map legacy children before schema filtering**  When a Memotron or Nucleum backup contains legacy `node.children`, this whitelist drops the field because the DataFn schema exposes only `mdChildOrder`, while `transformLegacyRecord()` has no node conversion. The separate `migrateDatafnNodeMdChildOrder()` pass runs before the recovery import and records its completion marker, so recovered markdown nodes permanent\nclient/persistence/legacyLocalDataBackup.ts\t1191\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Populate required objective defaults for PointGoal rows**  For old Pointron `PointGoal` rows, the retained `IPointGoal` shape has no `type` or `status` fields and instead may contain `isCompleted`, but this conversion only handles ancestry and layout. Both fields are required by the DataFn objective schema, so these rows are rejected as skipped and the startup recovery cannot complete; synthesize the historic\nclient/stores/account.store.ts\t878\t**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Read uploaded file metadata from DataFn**  For normal cloud uploads, this saves file metadata only through DataFn, but `fileStore` still extends the Flux-backed `ResourceStore`; consumers such as `DraggableMediaGridElement` later resolve saved IDs with `fileStore.refresh()`. The object supplied immediately after upload therefore renders initially, but after reopening or reloading the document the Flux lookup \nclient/components/settings/DataSettings.svelte\t293\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Await delivery before reporting a legacy backup**  In an embedded iOS or macOS settings flow, `downloadFromBlob()` performs an asynchronous native upload/handoff and can reject or return `false`, but this newly added path does not await it and immediately shows the success toast. Although the startup recovery path now validates the same helper, a failed manual legacy backup is still reported as delivered and \nclient/stores/appMenu/appMenu.store.ts\t74\t**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Roll back failed app-menu preference mutations**  When `datafn.kv.merge()` rejects or resolves with `{ ok: false }`—for example, in `sync-direct` mode during a transient remote failure—this method has already updated `appMenuLocal` and never checks or rolls back the mutation. Pinning, unpinning, or reordering menu items consequently appears successful but disappears on the next authoritative signal or reload;\nclient/components/settings/sync/SyncSettings.svelte\t31\tAn E2EE session can arrive from another device while this browser still has `DATAFN_OFFLINABILITY=\"false\"`. DataFn forces that session onto local storage, but disabling this switch without correcting the persisted flag leaves `resolveStoredAuthSessionState()` treating the device as non-offlinable, so the next offline launch rejects its cached cloud session.  <details><summary>Technical details</summary>  ````markdown # Keep E2EE offlinability and cached-session auth consistent  ## Affected sites\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a055c4-948d-7b90-8dbf-b059d8086b3b","create_time":1788146289.842148}}}
