ocument the Flux lookup has no corresponding file row and the attachment disappears; migrate those readers to DataFn or maintain a compatibility write until Flux is retired.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/648858933a7aa016bf4f2818dd2f2ea066192824/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3750},"formatted_output":"null\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Populate required objective defaults for PointGoal rows**\n\nFor old Pointron `PointGoal` rows, the retained `IPointGoal` shape has no `type` or `status` fields and instead may contain `isCompleted`, but this conversion only handles ancestry and layout. Both fields are required by the DataFn objective schema, so these rows are rejected as skipped and the startup recovery cannot complete; synthesize the historical defaults and translate `isCompleted` before import.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/648858933a7aa016bf4f2818dd2f2ea066192824/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\nnull\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Read uploaded file metadata from DataFn**\n\nFor normal cloud uploads, this saves file metadata only through DataFn, but `fileStore` still extends the Flux-backed `ResourceStore`; consumers such as `DraggableMediaGridElement` later resolve saved IDs with `fileStore.refresh()`. The object supplied immediately after upload therefore renders initially, but after reopening or reloading the document the Flux lookup has no corresponding file row and the attachment disappears; migrate those readers to DataFn or maintain a compatibility write until Flux is retired.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L12-L13](https://github.com/21nCo/nucleum/blob/648858933a7aa016bf4f2818dd2f2ea066192824/AGENTS.md#L12-L13)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n"},"started_at_ms"